daughters of three Ottoman Sultans:', 'node_id': '59c197ab-977f-4c8a-82be-2f799a5fd0d4', 'score': 1.000591516494751}, {'text': 'Esma Sultan (17 July 1778 – 4 June 1848) was an Ottoman princess, daughter of Sultan Abdul Hamid I, sister of Sultan Mustafa IV and Sultan Mahmud II. She was the adoptive mother of Bezmiâlem Sultan and Rahime Perestu Sultan.', 'node_id': '7cd80a80-1ddd-4685-b37a-9517d69eb805', 'score': 1.0091981887817383}, {'text': 'Esma Sultan (14 March 1726 – 13 August 1788) was an Ottoman princess, daughter of Sultan Ahmed III and his consort Zeynep Kadın. She was the half-sister of Sultan Mustafa III and Abdul Hamid I.', 'node_id': 'e543769a-b0bb-4955-aa4f-3465664c0636', 'score': 1.0283890962600708}, {'text': 'The Great Mosque of Algiers (Arabic: الجامع الكبير\u200e \u200e , "Jemaa Kebir") or “Djama’a al-Kebir” (meaning Great Mosque) is a mosque in Algiers, Algeria, located very close to Algiers Harbor. An inscription on the minbar (منبر) or the pulpit testifies to fact that the mosque was built in 1097.', 'node_id': 'e23a37a2-fac0-4914-be21-408673891897', 'score': 1.0338943004608154}, {'text': "It is also known by several other names such as Grand Mosque d'Alger, Djamaa al-Kebir, El Kebir Mosque and Jami Masjid. It is one of the few remaining examples of Almoravid architecture. It is the oldest mosque in Algiers and is said to be the oldest mosque in Algeria after Sidi Okba Mosque. It was built under sultan Ali ibn Yusuf. Its minaret dates from 1332 (1324 in some sources) and was built by the Ziyyanid Sultan of Tlemcen.", 'node_id': 'c1671449-a7c2-4cff-b05b-8e5468cc9375', 'score': 1.0523591041564941}, {'text': "New Palace, Kolhapur is a palace situated in Kolhapur, in the Indian state of Maharastra. It was constructed between 1877–1884. Being an excellent specimen of architecture built in black polished stone, it has been an attraction for tourists. It has extensive premises with a garden, fountain and wrestling ground. The whole building is eight-angled and has a tower in the middle. The clock on it was fixed in 1877. At separate distances there are small towers. On every glass are painted the events in Shivaji's life.", 'node_id': '6e918aeb-45fe-43fa-8da2-7dd671416df3', 'score': 1.1401479244232178}], 'consistency_check': 'CONSISTENT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 1.0705083440989256, 'vram_usage': 1.21240234375}
