  1%|          | 5/500 [00:43<1:29:07, 10.80s/it]  1%|          | 6/500 [00:52<1:24:49, 10.30s/it]['Eenasul Fateh'] {'response': 'Eenasul Fateh, also known by his stage name Aladin, is the individual referred to in your question. He is a Bangladeshi-British cultural practitioner, magician, and live artist. Additionally, he has experience as a former international management consultant, which implies that he helped organizations improve their performance in that capacity. Therefore, Eenasul Fateh is the person known by the stage name Aladin who also contributed to organizational performance as a consultant.', 'query': 'Who was known by his stage name Aladin and helped organizations improve their performance as a consultant?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Eenasul Fateh (Bengali: ঈনাসুল ফাতেহ ; born 3 April 1959), also known by his stage name Aladin, is a Bangladeshi-British cultural practitioner, magician, live artist and former international management consultant.', 'node_id': '8a606432-b505-4dd9-b23f-31d40c482542', 'score': 0.9520035982131958}, {'text': 'Claudio Fernández-Aráoz is an Argentinian author, international speaker and global expert on talent and leadership, ranked by "BusinessWeek" as one of the most influential executive search consultants in the world. He is currently a senior adviser of Egon Zehnder. Before joining Egon Zehnder in 1986, he worked at McKinsey & Company in Europe. He is a frequent lecturer at the Harvard Business School.', 'node_id': '4d54cdbd-cfcf-4251-a85d-ddd9f9125ac1', 'score': 1.041841745376587}, {'text': 'He is also co-founder and co-Editor-in-Chief of "Healthcare: The Science of Delivery and Innovation", consulting professor of medicine at the Stanford University School of Medicine, and a Contributor at Forbes.', 'node_id': 'f1f19aad-5a05-4f14-812f-cd4e661c69fa', 'score': 1.0922577381134033}, {'text': 'He was a member of the advisory panel of Lloyds Pharmacy until April 2010 and a senior adviser to DAM Capital until December 2009, to Centrica plc until 2012 and to Celesio AG. He was educated at Dover College and New College, Oxford where he won a blue for Rugby.', 'node_id': 'a09af109-b44b-49e7-9cdb-b61d21d40104', 'score': 1.2200909852981567}, {'text': 'In addition, he is a Dramatists Guild "Traveling Master", teaching workshops and master classes on playwriting and story-making around the U.S.', 'node_id': '955e4b74-02ca-43a5-9688-00469779a786', 'score': 1.229348063468933}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 1.1942405495792627, 'vram_usage': 1.24755859375}
