['yes'] {'response': 'The provided context is insufficient regarding Ambroise Thomas. It does not mention him or provide information about his status as an opera composer. However, it does confirm that Giuseppe Verdi is an opera composer, known for his significant contributions to the operatic repertoire. Therefore, while we can affirm that Verdi is an opera composer, we cannot determine the status of Ambroise Thomas based on the provided context.', 'query': 'Are Giuseppe Verdi and Ambroise Thomas both Opera composers ?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Ferrani sang a wide repertoire that encompassed not only verismo opera but the works of composers like Verdi, Gounod, Wagner, and Debussy.', 'node_id': '570db187-c75d-4eeb-b05f-1f02477907a6', 'score': 0.892401933670044}, {'text': 'Ferdinando Angelo Maria Provesi (1770 – 1833) was a native of Parma, Italy. He was regarded as one of the greatest Italian opera composers of the era . Provesi is best known as being an early tutor of Giuseppe Verdi when he was the "Maestro di cappella" (master of music) at the St. Bartolomeo cathedral in Busseto (the town very close to Le Roncole, the village where Verdi was born.)', 'node_id': '1db71a05-acba-40e8-908a-5c0f97ddb2d1', 'score': 0.9239654541015625}, {'text': 'Giuseppe Verdi is a 1938 Italian biographical film directed by Carmine Gallone and starring Fosco Giachetti, Gaby Morlay and Germana Paolieri. The film portrays the life of the composer Giuseppe Verdi (1813-1901). The casting of Giachetti as Verdi was intended to emphasise the composer\'s patriotism, as he had recently played patriotic roles in films such as "The White Squadron". The film was made at the Cinecittà Studios in Rome. The film is also known by the alternative title The Life of Giuseppe Verdi.', 'node_id': '0d7880b3-b35e-45ee-8083-f51a551193aa', 'score': 0.9247053265571594}, {'text': 'Giuseppe Verdi, released theatrically in the USA as The Life and Music of Giuseppe Verdi and on video as Verdi, the King of Melody, is a 1953 Italian biographical film starring Pierre Cressoy and directed by Raffaello Matarazzo. It is based on adult life events of the composer Giuseppe Verdi. The film was a commercial success, grossing over 957 million lire at the Italian box office.', 'node_id': '30af6eb6-af75-4e31-b5c4-cbda560f866c', 'score': 0.9336042404174805}, {'text': 'This list provides a guide to opera composers, as determined by their presence on a majority of compiled lists of significant opera composers. (See the "Lists Consulted" section for full details.) The composers run from Jacopo Peri, who wrote the first ever opera in late 16th century Italy, to John Adams, one of the leading figures in the contemporary operatic world. The brief accompanying notes offer an explanation as to why each composer has been considered major. Also included is a section about major women opera composers, compiled from the same lists. For an introduction to operatic history, see opera.', 'node_id': 'd8e34033-9f59-41fc-98af-951fdaecc98f', 'score': 0.9669283628463745}, {'text': 'Provesi was also director of the municipal music school and local Philharmonic Society. He began teaching Verdi in 1824 when the future composer was 11 years old.', 'node_id': 'ec8dd32e-3d0f-4d07-bd26-9b8cdc61f8a1', 'score': 0.9696435928344727}, {'text': 'For an introduction to operatic history, see opera. The organisation of the list is by birthdate.', 'node_id': '096f4fbd-94e9-45fa-b243-1f14af395a5c', 'score': 1.017890453338623}, {'text': 'His stage repertoire included Belmonte in Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart\'s "Die Entführung aus dem Serail", Chapelou in Adolphe Adam\'s "Le postillon de Lonjumeau", Count Almaviva in Gioachino Rossini\'s "The Barber of Seville", Daniel in Franz Lehár\'s "The Merry Widow", the Duke of Mantua in Giuseppe Verdi\'s "Rigoletto", Gabriel von Eisenstein in Johann Strauss II\'s "Die Fledermaus", Indigo in Strauss\' "Indigo und die vierzig Räuber",', 'node_id': '0bf5907e-220b-4b51-92ac-b2032af37842', 'score': 1.0271646976470947}, {'text': 'Lorenzo Ratti (ca. 1589–1630) was an Italian baroque composer. He was the predecessor of Carissimi at the Collegium Germanicum. He composed six Gospel Dialogues for the oratory. He was a teacher of Benevoli.', 'node_id': 'd515debe-2949-4a20-b65d-a901993c604c', 'score': 1.0410828590393066}, {'text': 'Tomaso Giovanni Albinoni (8 June 1671 – 17 January 1751) was an Italian Baroque composer. While famous in his day as an opera composer, he is mainly remembered today for his instrumental music, such as the concerti.', 'node_id': 'b1e96ed7-f531-4d5c-bbc7-3d5a4998ca5f', 'score': 1.0457738637924194}], 'consistency_check': 'CONFLICT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 1.057345848530531, 'vram_usage': 1.16552734375}
