  4%|▎         | 18/500 [02:50<1:00:57,  7.59s/it]  4%|▍         | 19/500 [02:55<52:49,  6.59s/it]    4%|▍         | 20/500 [03:01<51:49,  6.48s/it]  4%|▍         | 21/500 [03:04<44:39,  5.59s/it]  4%|▍         | 22/500 [03:09<42:02,  5.28s/it]  5%|▍         | 23/500 [03:12<36:27,  4.59s/it]['Badly Drawn Boy'] {'response': 'The provided context is insufficient regarding the performance act of Wolf Alice and their instrument to person ratio. It only provides information about Badly Drawn Boy and does not mention Wolf Alice or any relevant details to compare the two acts.', 'query': 'Which performance act has a higher instrument to person ratio, Badly Drawn Boy or Wolf Alice? ', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': "The film's plot centers on Alice, an 11-year-old girl starting the sixth grade at a new school. It was starring Alyson Stoner, Lucas Grabeel, Bridgit Mendler, Luke Perry, Penny Marshall and Ashley Eckstein.", 'node_id': '78ea605d-fa8d-4ef8-90b8-258a023ffb0c', 'score': 1.3319470882415771}, {'text': 'The Hour of Bewilderbeast is the debut studio album by British musician Badly Drawn Boy, released on 26 June 2000. Damon Gough, who performs as Badly Drawn Boy, wrote, produced, and played several instruments on the album\'s eighteen tracks, several of which also feature accompaniment by members of the British indie rock bands Alfie and Doves. "The Hour of Bewilderbeast" was released to great critical acclaim and went on to win the 2000 Mercury Prize, and has sold 455,000 copies in the United Kingdom as of September 2011.', 'node_id': '10cd8c08-5df6-4acc-bddb-47a4f940f972', 'score': 1.3388839960098267}, {'text': 'About a Boy is the second album by English singer-songwriter Badly Drawn Boy, released in 2002 under Twisted Nerve Records and XL Recordings, and in America under the short-lived ARTISTdirect Records, as the soundtrack to the film "About a Boy". Gough was chosen to compose and perform the entire soundtrack.', 'node_id': '4c021ab7-5b3a-471d-9c5a-430d8d095dfc', 'score': 1.3470444679260254}, {'text': "The band's double-set performance, which included several blues and R&B standards, was highly successful, receiving mostly positive reviews from music critics.", 'node_id': '32a4f2b4-2b38-496e-9eed-d8a7fb8d6954', 'score': 1.3733251094818115}, {'text': 'She continues to direct, most recently "L\'etoile" and "The Marriage of Figaro" for the Wolf Trap Opera Festival, " La Calisto", "The Magic Flute" and "Iphigénie en Aulide" for Juilliard Opera Center, and at Gotham Chamber Opera, "Il Signor Bruschino". She currently holds the J. Ralph Corbett Distinguished Chair in Opera at the University of Cincinnati College-Conservatory of Music."', 'node_id': 'c531ab3a-1c34-4059-b30b-77d5a8443658', 'score': 1.3944272994995117}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 0.7763943634927273, 'vram_usage': 1.23583984375}
