  7%|▋         | 35/500 [05:15<2:13:40, 17.25s/it]  7%|▋         | 36/500 [05:20<1:44:15, 13.48s/it]['2000'] {'response': 'The provided context is insufficient regarding the year that Carlo Rovelli, the author of "Seven Brief Lessons on Physics," began working in France.', 'query': 'Seven Brief Lessons on Physics was written by an Italian physicist that has worked in France since what year?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Seven Brief Lessons on Physics (Italian: "" ) is a short book by the Italian physicist Carlo Rovelli. Originally published in Italian in 2014, the book has been translated into 41 languages. It is an Italian bestseller, with more than 300,000 copies sold in Rovelli\'s home country.', 'node_id': 'e95866d6-ed7f-42e6-9d37-965edc72d942', 'score': 0.4300316572189331}, {'text': 'Chiara R. Nappi is an Italian physicist. Her research areas have included mathematical physics, particle physics, and string theory.', 'node_id': '798ecaa2-6ac3-4eb0-9c35-e1bbf0cd5e0a', 'score': 0.8644665479660034}, {'text': 'Luciano Pietronero (born in Rome on December 15, 1949) is an Italian physicist (statistical physics) and full professor at the department of Physics at University of Rome "Sapienza".', 'node_id': '8806e528-51ee-4d16-868e-4d1733b4f0af', 'score': 0.9238017201423645}, {'text': 'Guido Caldarelli (born in Rome on 8 April 1967) is an Italian physicist (statistical physics) and full professor in Theoretical Physics at IMT School for Advanced Studies Lucca. He is married with two children and lives in Lucca.', 'node_id': '3ee32454-38a2-4c21-a201-93edcbb88fde', 'score': 1.034704566001892}, {'text': 'Aldo Pontremoli (] ; 19 January 1896 – 25 May 1928) was an Italian physicist who held a chair of theoretical physics at the University of Milan from 1926 and who founded and directed the Institute of Advanced Physics at the University of Milan from 1924 until his disappearance and presumed death in May 1928. Pontremoli was one of the six men who disappeared with the airborne envelope of the airship "Italia" after it had crashed on the Arctic ice on 25 May 1928.', 'node_id': 'b487757b-cc88-428b-9de7-cd25fd8b326c', 'score': 1.0365712642669678}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 1.0448818355798721, 'vram_usage': 1.25927734375}
