  7%|▋         | 37/500 [05:30<1:34:27, 12.24s/it]['World War II'] {'response': 'The provided context is insufficient regarding the specific number of casualties in the wars commemorated by the Livesey Hall War Memorial. However, it does state that the memorial commemorates the fallen of World War I and World War II, which are the two wars in question. World War II is known to have had over 60 million casualties, but the context does not provide specific details about the casualty figures.', 'query': 'The Livesey Hal War Memorial commemorates the fallen of which war, that had over 60 million casualties?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'The Livesey Hall War Memorial commemorates the fallen of World War I and World War II who had been employed by the South Suburban Gas Company of London. It is also a tribute to those employees who served in the wars. The monument was designed and executed by British sculptor Sydney March, of the March family of artists.', 'node_id': 'e28ce640-e463-4594-b1fd-2ab56ca53654', 'score': 0.6039342880249023}, {'text': 'The Alamein Memorial is a Commonwealth War Graves Commission war memorial in the El Alamein War Cemetery, El Alamein, Egypt. The memorial commemorates 11,866 Commonwealth forces members who died during World War II. The memorial was designed by Hubert Worthington and unveiled by Viscount Montgomery of Alamein on 24 October 1954.', 'node_id': 'ead8b3c0-87cb-4ba5-bd06-c997adeb401f', 'score': 0.9071599841117859}, {'text': 'The War Memorial in Hanoi is located across the Ba Dinh Square, across the Ho Chi Minh Mausoleum and close to Hanoi Citadel. Constructed in 1993 in a fusion of traditional Vietnamese and modernist architecture, the memorial commemorates men and women who sacrificed themselves during the Second Indochina War. The war is known by many names, e.g. as the American War in Vietnam. The memorial is a focal point for state functions, commemorating the war dead.', 'node_id': '69b1d85d-d194-4a0b-8452-1f4c6a1bdfd7', 'score': 0.9282110929489136}, {'text': 'The Rainham War Memorial commemorates soldiers killed in both World Wars as well as civilian casualties of World War II.', 'node_id': '39fd7193-4852-4d46-8d94-7e7a9d815d11', 'score': 0.930161714553833}, {'text': 'The Freetown Memorial is a Commonwealth War Graves Commission war memorial located outside the Secretariate Building in Freetown, Sierra Leone. The memorial generally commemorates Soldiers from Sierra Leone who died whilst serving with the Royal West African Frontier Force in West Africa and whose graves are not known. The Freetown Memorial commemorates 1,109 First World War casualties and 247 from the Second World War.', 'node_id': 'efd8a303-7374-45b7-97ea-588e1b4e481e', 'score': 1.0312196016311646}], 'consistency_check': 'CONSISTENT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 0.9599627889692783, 'vram_usage': 1.25927734375}
