d8d1ba785f', 'score': 0.6253114938735962}, {'text': "Dirleton (Scottish Gaelic 'Duighreach') is a village and parish in East Lothian, Scotland approximately 20 mi east of Edinburgh on the A198. It contains 7500 acre . Dirleton lies between North Berwick (east), Gullane (west), Fenton Barns (south) and the Yellowcraigs nature reserve, Archerfield Estate and the Firth of Forth (north).", 'node_id': 'aa8ea192-e7a6-47b2-9367-8559c0363289', 'score': 0.766471803188324}, {'text': 'Dirleton Kirk is situated to the north of the village green in Dirleton, in East Lothian, Scotland. Dirleton village lies on the south shore of the Firth of Forth 21 miles east of Edinburgh and two miles west of North Berwick on the A198 road. The church is at grid reference [ NT512842] .', 'node_id': '7897393c-1b89-49bb-b430-e25b03f537ea', 'score': 0.7779014110565186}], 'consistency_check': 'CONSISTENT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 3.1024501733481884, 'vram_usage': 1.28271484375}
