  9%|▉         | 46/500 [06:55<1:37:09, 12.84s/it]['Phil Spector'] {'response': 'The provided context is insufficient regarding the writer of the song inspired by words on a tombstone that was the first track on the box set Back to Mono.', 'query': 'Who is the writer of this song that was inspired by words on a tombstone and was the first track on the box set Back to Mono?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'The track was described by the band as their "love letter to being home," having written the song after returning to their native Wales after recording in Los Angeles.', 'node_id': 'bc74c7f3-4f8e-4368-85c9-2830fce0757b', 'score': 1.0542627573013306}, {'text': 'The first track of the box set is the Buddy Holly-produced "Jole Blon," released in 1958, while the last is "I Do Believe," a song produced by Don Was that was included on The Highwaymen\'s 1995 release, "The Road Goes on Forever". The other material on the box set covers Jennings\' career chronologically, with songs ranging from his years on RCA\'s roster to later compositions from his short-lived stay at Epic Records; it ignores, however, the tracks from Jennings albums released on independent labels.', 'node_id': 'e7864ae7-b685-49c5-9c1c-d7543deac809', 'score': 1.0570687055587769}, {'text': 'The song was produced by Edward "Eddie F" Ferrell and Darren Lighty for Untouchables Entertainment. It is Jones\'s biggest hit to date. The song was co-written by Anthony Hamilton. The songs serves as the opening track on LaFace Records.', 'node_id': '8ddc3d0c-ed89-4b28-b7b4-8bf88e5d9850', 'score': 1.0607059001922607}, {'text': "The show's title relates to the song of the same name, written by Sid Tepper and Roy C. Bennett, and sung by Cliff Richard and The Shadows, which was a No. 1 UK hit single.", 'node_id': 'e5c57d13-2c04-4885-a458-f2bbaeacb1b5', 'score': 1.0747822523117065}, {'text': "The music video was unveiled at 3PM on January 1, 2009 on The N. Bassist/lyricist Pete Wentz commented that the song was about society's fixation with celebrities. The music was composed by vocalist/guitarist Patrick Stump.", 'node_id': '517b4dad-cb4d-466a-95cd-392d9107b48d', 'score': 1.0917437076568604}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 0.666704474017024, 'vram_usage': 1.35302734375}
