['Ronald Shusett'] {'response': 'The provided context is insufficient regarding the name of the executive producer of the film that has a score composed by Jerry Goldsmith.', 'query': 'What is the name of the executive producer of the film that has a score composed by Jerry Goldsmith?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'The original score composed by Jerry Goldsmith won the BMI Film Music Award.', 'node_id': '4ae865b0-879d-4e5f-8f9b-d83561b6aca6', 'score': 0.5228481292724609}, {'text': 'Legend: The Music of Jerry Goldsmith is a musical film score by American composer Jerry Goldsmith, released in 1986 for the worldwide release of the film of the same name, (excluding the US). The album was released on compact disc in 1992 through Silva Screen records and featured alternate cover art and additional songs.', 'node_id': 'a3d8888b-8e26-449c-b323-22c7fa1e98eb', 'score': 0.528109073638916}, {'text': 'Additional cues taken from Jerry Goldsmith\'s "Alien" score were used in the climax of the film when Horner was unable to finish some cues to Cameron\'s satisfaction. The film\'s editors also reportedly altered the score\'s chronological flow, sometimes looping, truncating or removing the music and placing it in fragmented form in the film out of context. Despite production issues, it was nominated for an Academy Award in 1986. It was performed by the London Symphony Orchestra. The soundtrack album was released the following year, in 1987.', 'node_id': '56862f69-e1b3-40c6-a8df-a4d037fcff0e', 'score': 0.8606961965560913}, {'text': 'The iconic, avant-garde score to the film "Alien" was composed by Jerry Goldsmith and is considered by some to be one of his best, most visceral scores. Rather than focusing on themes, Goldsmith creates a bleak and dissonant soundscape that fits the film\'s dark and intense atmosphere, with only a few "romantic" cues.', 'node_id': 'ce996b09-fffb-4f19-b712-7e02153fbe1d', 'score': 0.8633745908737183}, {'text': 'The screenplay was written by John Sayles, the score was composed by James Horner, and the special effects were designed by James Cameron.', 'node_id': '10ca249f-e2a2-41bc-a7d3-29a0b498d502', 'score': 0.9202984571456909}, {'text': 'Steven Katz is the supervising producer and also writer, Michael Polaire is the producer and David Kirchner is the associate producer.', 'node_id': '051d8ea3-3f74-42fd-a82c-93c1d76a707b', 'score': 1.038370132446289}, {'text': 'Other films as a director include "The Boys of Baraka", "Freakonomics", and "The Education of Mohammed Hussein".', 'node_id': '955edb41-aabc-4980-8d80-9f217d67f061', 'score': 1.0852172374725342}, {'text': 'The score to the 1986 James Cameron film "Aliens" was composed by James Horner. The score itself includes musical references to Gayane\'s Adagio from Aram Khachaturian\'s "Gayane" ballet suite, which had been used in Stanley Kubrick\'s "" (1968). The score also uses musical motifs, sound treatments and excerpts from Jerry Goldsmith\'s original soundtrack to "Alien" (1979).', 'node_id': 'd4a3ba6b-3e4f-4ed2-acc0-0d7e6b80025e', 'score': 1.103029489517212}, {'text': 'The film is directed by Zack Snyder and written by Chris Terrio and Joss Whedon, from a story by Snyder and Terrio, and features an ensemble cast that includes Ben Affleck, Henry Cavill, Gal Gadot, Jason Momoa, Ezra Miller, Ray Fisher, Ciarán Hinds, Amy Adams, Willem Dafoe, Jesse Eisenberg, Jeremy Irons, Diane Lane, Connie Nielsen, and J. K. Simmons.', 'node_id': '17a16328-07c7-441c-ac86-86f2b01c07ef', 'score': 1.1178555488586426}, {'text': '127 Hours: Music from the Motion Picture is the soundtrack to Danny Boyle\'s 2010 film of the same name. It was composed by two-time Academy Award Winner A. R. Rahman, Boyle\'s previous collaborator on "Slumdog Millionaire". The score, centred on guitar, was recorded mainly in London and was completed in three weeks. The soundtrack was released digitally on 2 November and physically on 22 November, by Interscope Records. The score is briefly orchestral and the song\'s main theme, "If I Rise" features Rahman playing the Harpejji.', 'node_id': '2c0f9219-316d-404e-9607-f8da406c6faa', 'score': 1.131142020225525}, {'text': "This is the first film that Smith directed that he did not also write. Upon its release, the film was met with negative reviews by critics and underperformed at the box office. It is nevertheless Kevin Smith's highest grossing film.", 'node_id': 'a96719f2-b5ec-4305-ba58-aa42ea4e8079', 'score': 1.1555290222167969}, {'text': '"Lost", "Lies" and "Can\'t Happen Here" were used in the film "Mortal Kombat", but Stabbing Westward refused to include it in the official soundtrack. The "Thread Mix" of "Violent Mood Swings" was included in the Clerks soundtrack.', 'node_id': '3eaec51e-be21-4baa-9779-7494b498970d', 'score': 1.1618479490280151}, {'text': 'Dev has cited Prince, Hercules & The Love Affair and Gary Utteridge amongst his musical influences.', 'node_id': 'c2092f2f-4c07-4276-b1d6-02ad4e6e2a7c', 'score': 1.1856895685195923}, {'text': '", "The Rockford Files", "MADtv", and "The Suite Life on Deck", as well as such movie productions as "When Harry Met Sally..." and "The Player". It was previously known as Hollywood Center Studios.', 'node_id': '7cda19be-d2e3-4a10-8129-496359fa60bd', 'score': 1.1941044330596924}, {'text': 'Also of note are his plays "Ninth and Joanie" directed by Mark Wing-Davey, produced in New York City by LAByrinth Theater Company, "Roger and Vanessa", produced at Theatre 503 in London, The Actors\' Gang in Los Angeles and Tap Gallery in Sydney and "Unconditional", produced by LAByrinth at NYC\'s Public Theater, directed by Mark Wing-Davey and published in "New Playwrights: The Best Plays of 2008".', 'node_id': '7d810710-cc44-422b-9227-af2298c338d8', 'score': 1.2196072340011597}, {'text': 'Neil N. LaBute (born March 19, 1963) is an American film director, screenwriter, playwright and actor. He is best-known for a play that he wrote and later turned into a film, "In the Company of Men" (1997), which won awards from the Sundance Film Festival, the Independent Spirit Awards, and the New York Film Critics Circle. He wrote and directed the films "Possession" (2002) (based on the A.S.', 'node_id': '8a010d27-0d6e-4fd6-96e0-d4ef21d272d4', 'score': 1.2264719009399414}, {'text': '"Detropia", a poetic look at Ewing\'s home town, also won several awards, including Best Editing at Sundance 2012, Outstanding Direction and Outstanding Original Score, at the 2013 Cinema Eye Honors for Nonfiction Filmmaking and a News and Documentary Emmy for editing. "Norman Lear: Just Another Version of You" was the opening night selection of the 2016 Sundance Film Festival and premiered on PBS American Masters on October 25, 2016.', 'node_id': '2450cb00-73eb-435a-96e0-468735764233', 'score': 1.2312257289886475}, {'text': 'Rhett Reese is an American film producer, television producer and screenwriter. As a screenwriter, his credits include "Clifford\'s Really Big Movie", "Cruel Intentions 3". He has collaborated with Paul Wernick, writing the films "Zombieland", "", and "Deadpool". Together they also created the reality series "The Joe Schmo Show".', 'node_id': '1a029b22-25f8-4e57-ad81-ddc5df113f82', 'score': 1.232633352279663}, {'text': 'Delicatessen is a 1991 French post-apocalyptic black comedy film directed by Jean-Pierre Jeunet and Marc Caro, starring Dominique Pinon and Karin Viard. It was released in North America as "presented by Terry Gilliam." Like its successor, "The City of Lost Children" (1995), it was an homage to the works of Gilliam.', 'node_id': '2fe64451-a613-4f4b-9b43-a76a6c30ced0', 'score': 1.2349741458892822}, {'text': 'He also directed several episodes for shows such as "Hell on Wheels" and "Billions".', 'node_id': 'f6ea7e1c-9deb-4253-8d39-666b3bcf20d5', 'score': 1.2401760816574097}], 'consistency_check': 'CONFLICT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'ENTAILMENT', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 0.6821650303900242, 'vram_usage': 1.25927734375}
