 13%|█▎        | 64/500 [09:47<1:05:33,  9.02s/it]['more than 70 countries'] {'response': 'The provided context is insufficient regarding the number of countries in which ExxonMobil has operations.', 'query': 'Scott Parkin has been a vocal critic of Exxonmobil and another corporation that has operations in how many countries ?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Scott Parkin (born 1969, Garland, Texas is an anti-war, environmental and global justice organizer, former community college history instructor, and a founding member of the Houston Global Awareness Collective. He has been a vocal critic of the American invasion of Iraq, and of corporations such as Exxonmobil and Halliburton. Since 2006, he has worked as an campaigner for the Rainforest Action Network, organizing campaigns against Bank of America, Citibank, TXU and the Keystone XL Pipeline. He also organizes with Rising Tide North America.', 'node_id': '9cc0c2c8-d70d-4326-a214-50057cb4d446', 'score': 0.6900118589401245}, {'text': 'Gordon Johndroe (born 1974) is vice president of Government Operations Communications at The Boeing Company. He was named to this position in November 2014 and is responsible for developing and implementing communications strategies associated with advocacy for the company’s products and businesses, as well as issues management and outreach to the Washington, D.C. news media and related constituencies. Johndroe previously worked at Lockheed Martin from 2013-2014 as Vice President for Worldwide Media Relations.', 'node_id': 'f3366b83-d8a2-4530-9f7f-ddc419e7c653', 'score': 1.142085313796997}, {'text': 'Robert D. "Bob" Hormats (born April 13, 1943, in Baltimore, Maryland) is Vice Chairman of Kissinger Associates. Immediately prior he served as Under Secretary of State for Economic Growth, Energy, and the Environment (at the time, entitled Under Secretary of State for Economic, Business, and Agricultural Affairs) from 2009 to 2013. Hormats was formerly Vice Chairman of Goldman Sachs (International), which he joined in 1982.', 'node_id': 'd285b2f4-6aec-4eb5-b839-25d5f798aa8b', 'score': 1.1701760292053223}, {'text': 'Exxon was the brand name of oil and natural resources company Exxon Corporation, prior to 1972 known as Standard Oil Company of New Jersey. In 1999, Exxon Corporation merged with Mobil to form ExxonMobil. The "Exxon" brand is still used by ExxonMobil\'s downstream operations as a brand for certain of its gas stations, motor fuel and related products (the highest concentration of which are located in New Jersey, Pennsylvania, Texas and in the Mid-Atlantic and Southeastern states).', 'node_id': 'fd9847d0-dfce-48b8-8ad9-1381367b0ae2', 'score': 1.224621295928955}, {'text': 'He is a member of the American Federation of Television and Radio Artists.', 'node_id': '3036f65a-8fe7-4749-8bff-a1135677c2e3', 'score': 1.2364931106567383}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 0.8525968920439482, 'vram_usage': 1.30615234375}
