 13%|█▎        | 67/500 [10:56<2:05:55, 17.45s/it]['Usher'] {'response': 'The provided context is insufficient regarding the singer whose song was released as the lead single from the album "Confessions" and had a popular song stuck behind for eight consecutive weeks.', 'query': 'What is the name of the singer who\'s song was released as the lead single from the album "Confessions", and that had popular song stuck behind for eight consecutive weeks?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'The album was preceded by the release of the lead single "Missing You" on 5 August 2010. It became the group\'s seventh top-ten hit when it peaked at number three in the UK and number six in Ireland.', 'node_id': '4248ee19-6b69-4694-ba9c-1d5c6b1048d3', 'score': 1.0585761070251465}, {'text': 'On the album Rise and Fall, Rage and Grace, it appears as the third track after Trust in You.', 'node_id': '5ed0974c-93ae-4777-929c-8d509bb3947d', 'score': 1.0651755332946777}, {'text': '"Numb" is a song by Barbadian singer Rihanna from her seventh studio album "Unapologetic" (2012). It features guest vocals by American rapper Eminem, making it the pair\'s third collaboration since the two official versions of "Love the Way You Lie". Following the album\'s release, "Numb" charted on multiple charts worldwide including in Canada, the United Kingdom and the United States.', 'node_id': 'eca235b0-b152-455f-8461-e8559d35cef6', 'score': 1.0693376064300537}, {'text': 'Long was also featured on The Notorious B.I.G.\'s hit song "Hypnotize", singing the chorus.', 'node_id': '3b54b392-f5d3-4f7f-aeb9-001674ea5735', 'score': 1.0829287767410278}, {'text': 'It peaked at #30 on the Australian singles charts. A remix version by [love] tatto was released on the Icehouse album "Meltdown" in 2002.', 'node_id': 'cef91e47-a727-48db-818c-5d52d3d2c0d0', 'score': 1.1149320602416992}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'CONTRADICTION'}, 'latency': 0.7522623185068369, 'vram_usage': 1.44677734375}
