 15%|█▌        | 75/500 [12:47<1:44:10, 14.71s/it]['John John Florence'] {'response': 'The provided context is insufficient regarding an American professional Hawaiian surfer born on 18 October 1992 who won the Rip Curl Pro Portugal.', 'query': 'What American professional Hawaiian surfer born 18 October 1992 won the Rip Curl Pro Portugal?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'MEO Rip Curl Pro Portugal formerly known as "Moche Rip Curl Pro Portugal" or "Rip Curl Pro Portugal" is a professional surfing competition of the ASP World Tour held every year in October at the Supertubos beach in Peniche, Portugal. The event was first founded in 2009 as "Rip Curl Search Portugal". The defending champion is the 2016 WSL champion, John John Florence who won the event in 2016.', 'node_id': '309821ef-3c92-4282-a67a-b554c6a0e23f', 'score': 0.7023905515670776}, {'text': "The MEO Rip Curl Pro Portugal 2016 was an event of the World Surf League for 2016 World Surf League Men's Championship Tour.", 'node_id': '4dc36084-2731-4fdd-8a6a-7da6c013f7a9', 'score': 0.7339975833892822}, {'text': "The MEO Rip Curl Pro Portugal 2017 is an event of the World Surf League for the 2017 World Surf League Men's Championship Tour.", 'node_id': '8b324b76-b890-44de-b000-79c3fb57dad9', 'score': 0.7571160793304443}, {'text': 'Coco Malia Camille Hapaikekoa Ho (born April 28, 1991) is a professional Hawaiian surfer born in Honolulu, Hawaii. She began surfing at 7 years old, following in the footsteps of her family. Today, Coco has won over 25 surfing awards and has been voted a top three fan favorite in Surfer magazine’s Surfer Poll.', 'node_id': '80a2f511-6b18-4834-9396-fe87b1124f88', 'score': 0.7826152443885803}, {'text': 'The Moche Rip Curl Pro Portugal 2015 was an event of the Association of Surfing Professionals for 2015 ASP World Tour.', 'node_id': '7242ac97-286a-4fa2-874d-c68fad839fde', 'score': 0.7903213500976562}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response