['John John Florence'] {'response': 'The provided context is insufficient regarding an American professional Hawaiian surfer born on October 18, 1992, who won the Rip Curl Pro Portugal.', 'query': 'What American professional Hawaiian surfer born 18 October 1992 won the Rip Curl Pro Portugal?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'MEO Rip Curl Pro Portugal formerly known as "Moche Rip Curl Pro Portugal" or "Rip Curl Pro Portugal" is a professional surfing competition of the ASP World Tour held every year in October at the Supertubos beach in Peniche, Portugal. The event was first founded in 2009 as "Rip Curl Search Portugal". The defending champion is the 2016 WSL champion, John John Florence who won the event in 2016.', 'node_id': '309821ef-3c92-4282-a67a-b554c6a0e23f', 'score': 20.812801361083984}, {'text': 'The Moche Rip Curl Pro Portugal 2015 was an event of the Association of Surfing Professionals for 2015 ASP World Tour.', 'node_id': '7242ac97-286a-4fa2-874d-c68fad839fde', 'score': 16.014074325561523}, {'text': 'The Moche Rip Curl Pro Portugal 2014 is an event of the Association of Surfing Professionals for 2014 ASP World Tour.', 'node_id': 'aea16915-38db-48b9-974c-8f299be2cd8b', 'score': 16.014074325561523}, {'text': "The MEO Rip Curl Pro Portugal 2017 is an event of the World Surf League for the 2017 World Surf League Men's Championship Tour.", 'node_id': '8b324b76-b890-44de-b000-79c3fb57dad9', 'score': 13.431346893310547}, {'text': "The MEO Rip Curl Pro Portugal 2016 was an event of the World Surf League for 2016 World Surf League Men's Championship Tour.", 'node_id': '4dc36084-2731-4fdd-8a6a-7da6c013f7a9', 'score': 13.431346893310547}, {'text': 'Damien Hardman (born January 23, 1966) known as The Iceman is a former Australian surfer from Sydney. He won the Rip Curl Pro twice in 1988 and 1993, and was runner-up three times in 1989, 1991 and 1997, and in 1987/88 and 1991 he won the ASP World Tour. In 1999, he was inducted into the Australian Surfing Hall of Fame in 1999.', 'node_id': 'dbd10567-5fff-406f-a182-158dc7a5c7c7', 'score': 12.320210456848145}, {'text': 'Barton Lynch (born August 9, 1963) is an Australian surfer known for his competitive prowess and style. In 1988, he was crowned ASP World Tour Champion. He also won the 1991 Rip Curl Pro. In 1998, he was inducted into the Australian Surfing Hall of Fame, and in 2000, he was inducted into the Australian Sporting Hall of Fame.', 'node_id': '6e1f249e-b000-4663-9769-1dd3a4d293b2', 'score': 12.29299259185791}, {'text': 'The Supertubos (Portuguese for "Supertubes") is a beach located in Peniche, Portugal, which due to its great conditions of surfing and its curvy waves and tubes helds every year the MEO Rip Curl Pro Portugal, one of the World Surf League Men\'s Championship Tour events.', 'node_id': '5fa62afa-c30a-4c8f-a591-1b88fffbe331', 'score': 11.963249206542969}, {'text': 'Over the course of his professional career, he won three world titles (2002, 2003, 2004), three Quiksilver Pro France titles (2003, 2004, 2005), two Rip Curl Pro Search titles (2006 and 2007) and 20 elite tour victories including the Vans Triple Crown of Surfing four times from 2002-2006. On September 3, 2010 he won the Billabong Pro Teahupoo in Tahiti.', 'node_id': '65bfe84e-554e-428e-93a4-ff7bf67022ee', 'score': 10.996099472045898}, {'text': 'Coco Malia Camille Hapaikekoa Ho (born April 28, 1991) is a professional Hawaiian surfer born in Honolulu, Hawaii. She began surfing at 7 years old, following in the footsteps of her family. Today, Coco has won over 25 surfing awards and has been voted a top three fan favorite in Surfer magazine’s Surfer Poll.', 'node_id': '80a2f511-6b18-4834-9396-fe87b1124f88', 'score': 10.733473777770996}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'CONTRADICTION'}, 'latency': 4.25790729932487, 'vram_usage': 0.0}
