['John Waters'] {'response': 'The provided context is insufficient regarding which American film director hosted the 18th Independent Spirit Awards in 2002.', 'query': 'Which American film director hosted the 18th Independent Spirit Awards in 2002?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Neil N. LaBute (born March 19, 1963) is an American film director, screenwriter, playwright and actor. He is best-known for a play that he wrote and later turned into a film, "In the Company of Men" (1997), which won awards from the Sundance Film Festival, the Independent Spirit Awards, and the New York Film Critics Circle. He wrote and directed the films "Possession" (2002) (based on the A.S.', 'node_id': '8a010d27-0d6e-4fd6-96e0-d4ef21d272d4', 'score': 10.928024291992188}, {'text': 'The 2012 Independent Spirit Awards was the 28th annual occasion of the Film Independent Spirit Awards. It announced its nominees on November 27, 2012. The winners were announced on February 23, 2013 during an awards ceremony hosted by Andy Samberg.', 'node_id': 'a143a299-c9f5-44eb-a2dc-785e646cea26', 'score': 10.497902870178223}, {'text': 'The Independent Spirit Award for Best First Feature is one of the annual Independent Spirit Awards. It is usually given to the director (or directors) and producer (or producers). The "first feature" designation is applied to the director not the producer(s). Therefore, producers have been nominated multiple times.', 'node_id': '38ddbfc6-2c99-4a1c-983b-86aed4df6e6e', 'score': 10.008231163024902}, {'text': 'The Independent Spirit Award for Best Film (or Best Feature) is one of the annual Independent Spirit Awards.', 'node_id': 'fea967a4-de49-423d-8ad6-c91f9bb29546', 'score': 10.005393028259277}, {'text': 'The Independent Spirit Award for Best Cinematography is one of the annual awards given by Independent Spirit Awards, a non-profit organization dedicated to independent film and independent filmmakers.', 'node_id': 'e0962e18-531e-4076-950e-71561c2cd6ab', 'score': 9.944046974182129}, {'text': 'The Independent Spirit Award for Best Editing is one of the annual awards given by Independent Spirit Awards, a non-profit organization dedicated to independent film and independent filmmakers.', 'node_id': 'e1406d50-ee55-4550-bb68-559befc3693d', 'score': 9.944046974182129}, {'text': 'The 32nd Independent Spirit Awards (2017) nominees were announced by Film Independent, the nonprofit arts organization that produces them, on November 22, 2016. The ceremony, hosted by Nick Kroll and John Mulaney, took place on Saturday, February 25, 2017, and was broadcast live on IFC at 2:00 pm PT. Online streaming service Sundance Now live-streamed the Spirit Awards concurrently with the telecast, with an on-demand version available on Sundance Now.', 'node_id': 'e872b9f2-ef97-4f3a-9715-bd4e0cbdefc9', 'score': 8.402095794677734}, {'text': 'The Film Independent Spirit Awards (abbreviated "Spirit Awards" and originally known as the FINDIE or Friends of Independents Awards), founded in 1984, are awards dedicated to independent filmmakers. Winners were typically presented with acrylic glass pyramids containing suspended shoestrings representing the paltry budgets of independent films. Since 2006, winners have received a trophy depicting a bird with its wings spread sitting atop of a pole with the shoestrings from the previous design wrapped around the pole.', 'node_id': 'f89948f4-c501-40d5-9788-378cb51107d2', 'score': 8.343473434448242}, {'text': 'The film was selected as the Mexican entry for the Best Foreign Language Oscar at the 80th Academy Awards, but it did not make the shortlist. The film was nominated for Best Foreign Film at the 24th Independent Spirit Awards. It gained nine nominations, including all major categories, in the Ariel Awards, the Mexican national awards.', 'node_id': 'c0f7588b-c2da-4930-ab9f-a43d92bf7e3d', 'score': 7.50740909576416}, {'text': 'Sebastian Mantilla is a director and screenwriter. In 2004, he directed the Cannes and Sundance selected short film, "Con diva" ("With Diva"). "Next to Babilonia" is his independent film about the Spanish mercenaries during the Iraq War, winner of Best Film award at Madrid Int\'l. At the 2008 Film Festival, he was given the Best Director award at the European Independent Film Festival 2009 and screened at "Cartagena Film Festival" in Colombia.', 'node_id': '6b12e204-5954-4678-be15-df0160fe22f1', 'score': 7.206240653991699}], 'consistency_check': 'CONFLICT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 3.986260937526822, 'vram_usage': 0.0}
