s Angeles. The film focuses on their day-to-day police work, their dealings with a certain group of gang members, their friendship with each other, and their personal relationships.', 'node_id': '21ce52b0-cbe3-4014-ad8e-50937752580f', 'score': 0.9429013729095459}, {'text': 'David Ayer (born January 18, 1968) is an American film director, producer, and screenwriter. He is best known for being the writer of "Training Day" (2001), and the director and writer of "Harsh Times" (2005), "Street Kings" (2008), "End of Watch" (2012), "Sabotage" (2014), "Fury" (2014), and "Suicide Squad" (2016).', 'node_id': '1b43f9df-9747-4aa4-b2ab-16ce2ea14c83', 'score': 0.9548419117927551}, {'text': 'Suicide Kings is a 1997 American mystery crime film based on Don Stanford\'s short story "The Hostage" and directed by Peter O\'Fallon. It stars Christopher Walken, Denis Leary, Sean Patrick Flanery, Johnny Galecki, Jay Mohr, Jeremy Sisto and Henry Thomas. The film follows the group of criminals who kidnap a respected Mafia figure. It has a 34% approval rating on Rotten Tomatoes and grossed $1.7 million in the US.', 'node_id': '3a16f29e-bb64-49e1-ab2c-c931fdf1a51a', 'score': 1.03125}], 'consistency_check': 'CONSISTENT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 1.2106304839253426, 'vram_usage': 1.55224609375}
