 32%|███▏      | 158/500 [25:52<55:25,  9.72s/it]['Manchester United'] {'response': "The football club that plays in the area between the old toll gates, Brooks's Bar and Trafford Bar, is Manchester United F.C. This club is located in the Old Trafford ward, which is part of the Metropolitan Borough of Trafford in Greater Manchester, England. Manchester United is one of the most famous football clubs in the world and has a rich history, having been managed by Sir Matt Busby from 1945 to 1969. The area is also home to Lancashire County Cricket Club, indicating a vibrant sports culture in Old Trafford.", 'query': 'What football club plays in the area between the old tool gates: Brook Bar and Trafford bar?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': "Old Trafford is an area of Stretford, in the Metropolitan Borough of Trafford, Greater Manchester, England, 2 mi southwest of Manchester city centre. The crossroads sites of two old toll gates roughly delineate the borders of the area: Brooks's Bar to the east and Trafford Bar to the west.", 'node_id': 'aa4cadfb-a390-41ca-a690-9b9a3fb6d11d', 'score': 0.7579004764556885}, {'text': "Trafford Bar is a tram stop on Greater Manchester's light rail system, Metrolink, at the junction of Talbot Road and Seymour Grove in Old Trafford. It opened on 15 June 1992 as part of Phase 1 of Metrolink's expansion, before which it was a railway station.", 'node_id': '517f9e91-1eea-4521-a861-8d8e9720f39d', 'score': 0.7840337753295898}, {'text': 'Gorse Hill is also the northernmost ward of Trafford council and is home to Trafford Town Hall, housing the council offices. Gorse Hill shares a border with Old Trafford ward, home to both Manchester United F.C. and Lancashire County Cricket Club.', 'node_id': 'c8e9d809-86a8-4b58-b3d4-d99a8e430e05', 'score': 0.9438749551773071}, {'text': 'The ground has terraces, a stand which was bought due to a fire which burnt the previous stands and a clubhouse which boasts a pub, a club shop open at match days and award-winning hospitality packages. The stadium is adjacent to the B4486 road, the Newchurch Road and the Ebbw River.', 'node_id': 'f4e01a9c-a507-42de-b337-2f64604478b8', 'score': 0.9690062999725342}, {'text': 'The Sir Matt Busby Sports Complex is a public leisure centre located in Bellshill, North Lanarkshire, Scotland. It is named in honour of Sir Matt Busby, the football manager who was born in Bellshill in 1909, managed Manchester United from 1945 to 1969 and died in 1994.', 'node_id': 'd11aa454-5d9e-41b1-841b-9e98f4cb9fc5', 'score': 1.0480985641479492}], 'consistency_check': 'CONSISTENT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 1.5457730274647474, 'vram_usage': 1.24755859375}
