 Hersey once recalled meeting Bedford-Jones in Paris, where he was working on two novels simultaneously, each story on its own separate typewriter.", 'node_id': '125a9244-6ac3-4a1b-af87-542e461cb350', 'score': 1.063509464263916}, {'text': 'The "literary magazine" was written by Sean Kelly; the sports page was by Christopher Cerf; and the Principal\'s Letter and the "In Memorium" piece were both by Ed Subitzky.', 'node_id': 'a84ed35f-c10f-44b2-ac0e-8992ee214b15', 'score': 1.0897170305252075}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 0.692665159702301, 'vram_usage': 1.22412109375}
