 39%|███▉      | 197/500 [32:23<1:20:28, 15.94s/it]['Golden Valley, Minnesota,'] {'response': 'The provided context is insufficient regarding the city where Robert Smith founded General Mills.', 'query': ' Robert Smith founded the multinational company headquartered in what city?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Robert Smith (June 12, 1802 – December 21, 1867) was a U.S. Representative from Illinois, nephew of Jeremiah Smith and Samuel Smith of New Hampshire. Smith founded General Mills in 1856.', 'node_id': 'f1e6519d-2e8f-43e9-92a0-0a5c07fcd3bf', 'score': 0.750379204750061}, {'text': 'Grant Gordon Smith (born 5 May 1980 in Irvine) is a Scottish footballer midfielder. He is the son of former Rangers and Brighton & Hove Albion striker and former Scottish Football Association chief executive Gordon Smith.', 'node_id': '518dc7e0-28dc-46ff-9465-27e2d86dd36a', 'score': 0.9054800271987915}, {'text': 'Alexander Gordon Smith (27 February 1979, Norwich, England) is an author of children and Young Adult fiction.', 'node_id': 'abb7d20c-7ee7-48aa-9ab8-d5f804faaeaa', 'score': 1.0956470966339111}, {'text': 'Steel plant in Utah, much of the Pacific Coast steel market by the late 1950s. Its assets included steelmaking plants in Napa, California (that it acquired from Basalt Rock Company in 1955) and Fontana, California (now operated by California Steel Industries), and a former open-pit iron ore mine at Eagle Mountain, California. Steel manufactured was also used in Kaiser Motors.', 'node_id': 'f3ae91ab-18ec-4b39-840b-b3cd33c848ea', 'score': 1.106124997138977}, {'text': 'Mike Smith started as an A&R man at MCA Publishing as a scout in 1988, where he signed Blur, Levitation and scouted The Smashing Pumpkins.', 'node_id': '3ea3aa2d-2363-4f54-8748-ef3e2787e336', 'score': 1.132103443145752}], 'consistency_check': 'CONSISTENT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'CONTRADICTION'}, 'latency': 0.5422701966017485, 'vram_usage': 1.15380859375}
