 41%|████▏     | 207/500 [33:52<39:30,  8.09s/it]['Colonel Charles Hastings Judd'] {'response': "Colonel Charles Hastings Judd served as Chamberlain and Colonel of the military staff of King Kalākaua, who is often referred to as The Merrie Monarch. He traveled with King Kalākaua on his 1881 world tour. Additionally, George Walter Hunter Macfarlane also held the position of Colonel of the military staff of King Kalākaua and served as his final chamberlain. Both individuals played significant roles in the royal court of the Kingdom of Hawaii during King Kalākaua's reign.", 'query': 'Who was Chamberlain and Colonel of the military staff of The Merrie Monarch?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Colonel Charles Hastings Judd (September 8, 1835 – April 18, 1890) was an American businessman, rancher, courtier and politician of the Kingdom of Hawaii. He served as Chamberlain and Colonel of the military staff of King Kalākaua and traveled with the monarch on his 1881 world tour.', 'node_id': '1277e909-e9a5-4eb2-8c3a-7b5a8aaaed23', 'score': 1.02215576171875}, {'text': "His eldest son, the fourth Earl, represented Castle Rising and Maidstone in the House of Commons, and after entering the House of Lords on his father's death, served as Captain of the Yeomen of the Guard from 1783 to 1804 and as Lord Steward of the Household from 1804 to 1812.", 'node_id': '9309ace4-6801-4664-9a73-c83d253408ab', 'score': 1.078303575515747}, {'text': 'George Walter Hunter Macfarlane (March 1, 1849 – February 20, 1921) was a British businessman, courtier and politician of the Kingdom of Hawaii. He served Colonel of the military staff of King Kalākaua, traveling with the monarch on his 1881 world tour. He also served as his final chamberlain of king and was at his deathbed in 1891.', 'node_id': 'fd9986ba-151f-426c-9253-357257e86ecf', 'score': 1.1032418012619019}, {'text': 'George de Dunbar, 10th Earl of Dunbar and March (1338–1420), 12th Lord of Annandale and Lord of the Isle of Man, was "one of the most powerful nobles in Scotland of his time, and the rival of the Douglases."', 'node_id': 'e25a9d63-f8bd-469d-a5f7-2f278ca1a1f4', 'score': 1.1043365001678467}, {'text': 'Charles, Prince of Wales; Anne, Princess Royal; Prince Andrew, Duke of York; and Prince Edward, Earl of Wessex, and Sophie, Countess of Wessex, have all made several small tours in this fashion.', 'node_id': 'b3398c74-da15-40b9-8075-78f7b537ccd1', 'score': 1.127319574356079}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'ENTAILMENT', 'response': 'CONTRADICTION'}, 'latency': 1.3181896768510342, 'vram_usage': 1.20068359375}
