 42%|████▏     | 211/500 [34:42<52:52, 10.98s/it]['Jackson Storm'] {'response': 'Armie Hammer, who voices a character in "The Polar Bears," is also the voice of Jackson Storm in the 2017 film "Cars 3." In "Cars 3," Jackson Storm is a new generation racer who poses a challenge to the main character, Lightning McQueen. Therefore, Armie Hammer\'s involvement in both projects showcases his versatility as a voice actor in animated films.', 'query': 'The Polar Bears featuring the voice of Armie Hammer, is also the same voice actor for which character in Cars 3?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': "The Polar Bears is a 2012 3D computer animated short film presented by The Coca-Cola Company, produced by Ridley Scott, written by David Reynolds, and directed by John Stevenson. The film features the voices of Lin-Manuel Miranda, Armie Hammer, Jonathan Adams, and Megyn Price. The film is based on Coca-Cola's iconic polar bears and was released on the company's website and YouTube channel on December 31, 2012.", 'node_id': 'dfdb7626-0394-4afc-bbd1-23d3cea793e8', 'score': 0.8408617973327637}, {'text': 'Robin David Segal (born January 21, 1956), better known by the stage name Robby Benson, is an American actor, director, singer and educator. He is known as the voice of The Beast in the Disney animated film "Beauty and the Beast" and its numerous sequels and spin-offs, and for directing several episodes of the popular sitcom "Friends".', 'node_id': '08930ad2-08f2-4cd5-bba4-2e2886ddb144', 'score': 0.9684012532234192}, {'text': 'Armand Douglas "Armie" Hammer (born August 28, 1986) is an American actor. He is known for his portrayal of the Winklevoss twins in the film "The Social Network" (2010), Prince Andrew Alcott in "Mirror Mirror" (2012), the title character in the adventure film "The Lone Ranger" (2013), Mike in "Mine" (2016), and the voice role of Jackson Storm in 2017\'s Disney-Pixar Film "Cars 3".', 'node_id': '919e16d2-9aac-4316-b12e-a0ad34fa86f4', 'score': 0.9999697208404541}, {'text': 'Cars 3 is a 2017 American 3D computer-animated auto racing sports comedy adventure film produced by Pixar and released by Walt Disney Pictures. Directed by Brian Fee, the screenplay was written by Kiel Murray, Bob Peterson and Mike Rich. The film is a sequel to "Cars" and a stand-alone sequel to "Cars 2". The returning voices of Owen Wilson, Bonnie Hunt and Larry the Cable Guy are joined by Cristela Alonzo, Chris Cooper, Armie Hammer, Nathan Fillion, Kerry Washington and Lea DeLaria, in addition to a dozen NASCAR personalities.', 'node_id': '0c40837a-e85e-4c4f-bd2e-351e002793cf', 'score': 1.0729483366012573}, {'text': 'Andy Milder (born August 16, 1969) is an American actor and voice actor. He has appeared in such films as "Apollo 13", "Armageddon", "Rumor Has It…", "Frost/Nixon", "Transformers" and "Domino". He was a series regular on "Fame L.A."', 'node_id': 'a7eaed16-b862-418c-972a-c53e688bfce6', 'score': 1.1252281665802002}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 1.2814724668860435, 'vram_usage': 1.30615234375}
