 43%|████▎     | 214/500 [35:31<1:04:24, 13.51s/it]['Arthur Ignatius Conan Doyle'] {'response': "The provided context is insufficient regarding Penelope Lively's birth date. However, it does provide information about Arthur Conan Doyle, who was born on 22 May 1859. To determine who was born first, one would need to know Penelope Lively's birth date, which is not included in the context.", 'query': 'Who was born first, Arthur Conan Doyle or Penelope Lively?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Adrian Malcolm Conan Doyle (19 November 19103 June 1970) was the youngest son of Sir Arthur Conan Doyle and his second wife Jean, Lady Doyle or Lady Conan Doyle. He had two siblings, sister Jean and brother Denis, as well as two half-siblings, sister Mary and brother Kingsley.', 'node_id': 'f57e4272-34ca-411a-b359-93ce030017c3', 'score': 0.7710355520248413}, {'text': '14, no. 2 (Summer 2012), pp.\xa01,6,7 - a publication of The Friends of the Arthur Conan Doyle Collection, Toronto Public Libraries.', 'node_id': 'd6b65e5a-532d-49d6-91b4-01698d92287b', 'score': 0.8134295344352722}, {'text': 'Sherlock Holmes is a 1916 American silent film starring William Gillette as Arthur Conan Doyle\'s Sherlock Holmes. The film, which was directed by Arthur Berthelet, was produced by Essanay Studios in Chicago. It was adapted from the 1899 stage play of the same name, which was based on the stories, "A Scandal in Bohemia," "The Final Problem," and "A Study in Scarlet" by Arthur Conan Doyle.', 'node_id': 'efa16723-3a04-4149-a830-fed13017fea9', 'score': 1.0431361198425293}, {'text': 'Der Hund von Baskerville is a 1914 German silent film adaptation of Arthur Conan Doyle\'s "The Hound of the Baskervilles". This was the first film adaptation of the famed Conan Doyle novel. According to the website silentera.com, the film was considered lost, but has been rediscovered; the Russian Gosfilmofond film archive possesses a print, while the Filmmuseum München has a 35mm positive print.', 'node_id': '2ce3f97f-a415-48c9-aa6b-1668a127cbfa', 'score': 1.0638902187347412}, {'text': "Sir Arthur Conan Doyle's Sherlock Holmes, also known simply as Sherlock Holmes, is a British-American 2010 steampunk mystery film directed by Rachel Lee Goldenberg and produced by independent American film studio The Asylum. It features the Sherlock Holmes characters created by Sir Arthur Conan Doyle, though it follows an original plot. The film details an unrecorded case in which eccentric detective Holmes and his companion Dr. Watson investigate a series of unusual monster attacks and a plot to destroy London. Gareth David-Lloyd plays Dr. John Watson and Ben Syder, making his film debut, plays Sherlock Holmes.", 'node_id': '80850dc7-e4fe-4842-b906-b99d0b508361', 'score': 1.0909278392791748}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 1.273467866703868, 'vram_usage': 1.16552734375}
