 44%|████▍     | 220/500 [36:31<57:55, 12.41s/it]['Kimberly Couger "Kimmy" Schmidt'] {'response': 'Elizabeth Claire Kemper is known for playing the character Kimmy Schmidt in the Netflix series "Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt." This show, created by Tina Fey and Robert Carlock, features Kemper in the title role, where she has received critical acclaim for her performance. "Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt" is a comedy series that has been streaming on Netflix since March 6, 2015.', 'query': 'Which Netflix series "Unbreakable" character is Elizabeth Claire Kemper known for playing?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt is an American television sitcom created by Tina Fey and Robert Carlock, starring Ellie Kemper in the title role, that has streamed on Netflix since March 6, 2015. Originally set for a 13-episode first season on NBC for spring 2015, the show was sold to Netflix and given a two-season order.', 'node_id': '7041f969-05e6-464e-b9cf-0919bad1f8da', 'score': 0.7689819931983948}, {'text': '"Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt" is an American sitcom created by Tina Fey and Robert Carlock, starring Ellie Kemper in the title role, that has streamed on Netflix since March 6, 2015. Originally set for a 13-episode first season on NBC for spring 2015, the show was sold to Netflix and given a two-season order.', 'node_id': '9b9688a2-5f1a-40f7-98b7-0f8435df0264', 'score': 0.792900800704956}, {'text': 'Elizabeth Claire Kemper (born May 2, 1980) is an American actress and comedian. She gained prominence when she starred in the NBC series "The Office" as receptionist Erin Hannon for the final five seasons. After her role in "The Office", she was cast in a leading role as Kimmy Schmidt in the Netflix comedy series "Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt", for which she has received critical acclaim. Kemper is also known for her supporting roles in the films "Bridesmaids" (2011) and "21 Jump Street" (2012).', 'node_id': '306f19a5-b426-4db2-a42c-363aab39a260', 'score': 0.8330724239349365}, {'text': 'Unbreakable is a 2000 American superhero thriller film written, produced, and directed by M. Night Shyamalan, and starring Bruce Willis and Samuel L. Jackson, alongside Robin Wright and Spencer Treat Clark. The movie is the first installment in a trilogy. In "Unbreakable", a security guard named David Dunn survives a horrific train crash. After the incident, with the help of a manipulative disabled comic book shop owner named Elijah Price, he learns that he possesses superhuman powers.', 'node_id': 'f67fbf03-f3fb-420a-9364-09538e71dd6e', 'score': 0.9933139681816101}, {'text': 'Claire Temple is a character portrayed by Rosario Dawson in the television series of the Marvel Cinematic Universe (MCU), based on the comic characters Claire Temple and Night Nurse. A nurse who gives medical aid to vigilantes, she first appeared in the first season of "Daredevil" (2015–). Dawson then signed a deal to return for the second season of the series, as well as potentially appear in any other Marvel Netflix series. She has since reprised the role in "Jessica Jones", "Luke Cage", "Iron Fist", and "The Defenders".', 'node_id': '3e8b6198-c094-4c5e-b311-fa1599febd2b', 'score': 1.0884289741516113}], 'consistency_check': 'CONFLICT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'ENTAILMENT', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 1.389567306265235, 'vram_usage': 1.23583984375}
