['Kimberly Couger "Kimmy" Schmidt'] {'response': 'Elizabeth Claire Kemper is known for playing the character Kimmy Schmidt in the Netflix series "Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt." The show, created by Tina Fey and Robert Carlock, has been streaming on Netflix since March 6, 2015. Kemper\'s portrayal of Kimmy Schmidt has garnered her critical acclaim, making her a prominent figure associated with the series.', 'query': 'Which Netflix series "Unbreakable" character is Elizabeth Claire Kemper known for playing?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Elizabeth Claire Kemper (born May 2, 1980) is an American actress and comedian. She gained prominence when she starred in the NBC series "The Office" as receptionist Erin Hannon for the final five seasons. After her role in "The Office", she was cast in a leading role as Kimmy Schmidt in the Netflix comedy series "Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt", for which she has received critical acclaim. Kemper is also known for her supporting roles in the films "Bridesmaids" (2011) and "21 Jump Street" (2012).', 'node_id': '306f19a5-b426-4db2-a42c-363aab39a260', 'score': 14.822196960449219}, {'text': '"Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt" is an American sitcom created by Tina Fey and Robert Carlock, starring Ellie Kemper in the title role, that has streamed on Netflix since March 6, 2015. Originally set for a 13-episode first season on NBC for spring 2015, the show was sold to Netflix and given a two-season order.', 'node_id': '9b9688a2-5f1a-40f7-98b7-0f8435df0264', 'score': 9.792737007141113}, {'text': 'Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt is an American television sitcom created by Tina Fey and Robert Carlock, starring Ellie Kemper in the title role, that has streamed on Netflix since March 6, 2015. Originally set for a 13-episode first season on NBC for spring 2015, the show was sold to Netflix and given a two-season order.', 'node_id': '7041f969-05e6-464e-b9cf-0919bad1f8da', 'score': 9.695140838623047}, {'text': 'Claire Temple is a character portrayed by Rosario Dawson in the television series of the Marvel Cinematic Universe (MCU), based on the comic characters Claire Temple and Night Nurse. A nurse who gives medical aid to vigilantes, she first appeared in the first season of "Daredevil" (2015–). Dawson then signed a deal to return for the second season of the series, as well as potentially appear in any other Marvel Netflix series. She has since reprised the role in "Jessica Jones", "Luke Cage", "Iron Fist", and "The Defenders".', 'node_id': '3e8b6198-c094-4c5e-b311-fa1599febd2b', 'score': 8.556558609008789}, {'text': 'Azie Mira Dungey is an American actress, comedian and writer. She wrote and played the lead role in the comedic web series "Ask a Slave," and is currently, ". . .writing a book as a follow-up to the series." Dungey is also currently a writer for the Netflix series "Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt", produced by Tina Fey and Robert Carlock.', 'node_id': '84f6ece7-04d6-4d40-9aa7-bfc457c6c9c6', 'score': 8.166491508483887}, {'text': 'Sam Means is an American comedy writer. He won three Emmy awards for his work on "The Daily Show with Jon Stewart", and wrote for both "30 Rock" and "Parks and Recreation" on NBC. He is currently a writer and producer on the Netflix series "Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt".', 'node_id': '167d841e-626e-43e8-8505-b64033dc134a', 'score': 6.930912971496582}, {'text': 'The Punisher) in the Netflix series "Daredevil", and is set to reprise the latter role in the Netflix series "The Punisher".', 'node_id': '04375710-83c1-4bf8-9f1f-accf2474883d', 'score': 6.50632905960083}, {'text': 'Brenda Bennett (born Brenda Elizabeth Claire Siobhan; 24 January 1962) is a British-American singer from Scotland. She is best known as a member of the American group Vanity 6 who married the musician Prince\'s set-designer Roy Bennett, and then became Prince\'s "wardrobe mistress." She started off in a CBS Records band called Ken Lyon and Tombstone which toured with Mott the Hoople and Queen.', 'node_id': '438332b4-632c-4e73-91b7-7eaa8013b418', 'score': 5.818098545074463}, {'text': 'Elizabeth Claire Liddell (b. 24 May ?) is a Scottish pianist and composer. She was born in Glasgow and studied at the Royal Scottish Academy of Music and Drama in Glasgow and the Royal College of Music in London with Andrew Lloyd Webber.', 'node_id': 'ace80a8c-0c74-4f66-9746-7a288a59f8a8', 'score': 5.665866851806641}, {'text': 'Bolin (愽林 , Bó Lín ) is a major fictional character in Nickelodeon\'s animated television series "The Legend of Korra", which aired from 2012 to 2014. The character and the series, a sequel to "", were created by Michael Dante DiMartino and Bryan Konietzko. He is voiced by P. J. Byrne. Bolin is able to manipulate the classical element of earth, which is known as earthbending.', 'node_id': 'def134f8-74dc-42ad-bd98-8675d449c483', 'score': 5.452003002166748}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'ENTAILMENT', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 4.974587297067046, 'vram_usage': 0.0}
