cted, linear concourses (A, B & C).', 'node_id': 'ce29aae7-e91d-48b8-8165-bd2b324729be', 'score': 0.7662950158119202}, {'text': 'Denver International Airport (DEN), (IATA: DEN,\xa0ICAO: KDEN,\xa0FAA LID: DEN) , is an airport in Denver, Colorado, United States. At 33,531 acres (52.4 sq mi), it is the largest airport in the United States by total land area. Runway 16R/34L, with a length of 16000 ft , is the longest public use runway in the United States.', 'node_id': '189daef7-4f4e-4fd5-907d-dcaded742a0e', 'score': 0.8458884358406067}, {'text': "It is home to one of the world's busiest airports , Charlotte Douglas International Airport, and is also the Carolinas' largest manufacturing region. The Charlotte MSA is the largest in the Carolinas, and the fourth largest metropolitan area in the Southeastern region of the United States behind, Miami, Atlanta, and Tampa.", 'node_id': '040d1f75-79ca-4a51-bfae-4d1f4432b7ae', 'score': 0.859172523021698}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'CONTRADICTION'}, 'latency': 1.2220117077231407, 'vram_usage': 1.34130859375}
