 48%|████▊     | 241/500 [40:24<36:28,  8.45s/it]['Donna Paige Helmintoller'] {'response': 'The American actress and singer born in 1956 who recorded the song "Something There" for "Beauty and the Beast" is Donna Paige Helmintoller, better known as Paige O\'Hara. She voiced the character Belle in the film and was part of the main cast that performed the song. Paige O\'Hara\'s contributions to the film, particularly her role as Belle, have made her a notable figure in Disney\'s animated musical history.', 'query': 'What american actress/singer born in 1956 recorded the song Something there for beauty and the beast?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': '"Something There" is a song written by lyricist Howard Ashman and composer Alan Menken for Walt Disney Pictures 30th animated feature film "Beauty and the Beast" (1991). Sung by the majority of the film\'s main cast, the song was recorded by American actors Paige O\'Hara as Belle and Robby Benson as the Beast via voice over, featuring actors Jerry Orbach, Angela Lansbury and David Ogden Stiers as Lumiere, Mrs. Potts and Cogsworth, respectively.', 'node_id': '83623af8-41e3-4c89-a1af-eb1b711535bd', 'score': 0.7427352666854858}, {'text': 'Donna Paige Helmintoller, better known as Paige O\'Hara (born May 10, 1956), is an American actress, singer and painter. O\'Hara began her career as a Broadway actress in 1983 when she portrayed Ellie May Chipley in the musical "Showboat". In 1991, she made her motion picture debut in Disney\'s "Beauty and the Beast", in which she voiced the film\'s heroine, Belle.', 'node_id': '102538eb-a666-4910-88af-28ba7fa7fbb5', 'score': 0.852806806564331}, {'text': '"Beauty and the Beast" was subsequently recorded as a pop duet by Canadian singer Celine Dion and American singer Peabo Bryson, and released as the only single from the film\'s soundtrack on November 25, 1991.', 'node_id': '3ae5338f-8c28-47e5-a743-002730f49689', 'score': 0.8649693727493286}, {'text': 'Potts and Cogsworth, respectively. The only song performed by the Beast, "Something There" is heard midway through "Beauty and the Beast "during a scene in which Belle and the Beast finally begin to acknowledge their own feelings for each other.', 'node_id': 'c88e7ff5-cc64-4214-9393-66185641b46c', 'score': 0.8783913850784302}, {'text': '"Belle" is a song written by composer Alan Menken and lyricist Howard Ashman for Walt Disney Pictures\' 30th animated feature film "Beauty and the Beast" (1991). Originally recorded by American actress and singer Paige O\'Hara and American actor Richard White, "Belle", a mid-tempo French and classical music-inspired song, incorporates both Broadway and musical theatre elements.', 'node_id': 'f7c20a72-ba68-4876-9667-e42707d84529', 'score': 0.9564476013183594}], 'consistency_check': 'CONSISTENT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 1.5774703789502382, 'vram_usage': 1.24755859375}
