d in north part of Hohhot, the capital city of Inner Mongolia Autonomous Region.", 'node_id': '74343e7a-7875-46e4-831c-50a7984c7bc6', 'score': 1.2018224000930786}, {'text': "Construction began on June 30, 2014 and was slated to take three years, but the line opened only 17 months later on December 1, 2015. The opening of this rail line shortened the distance by rail from Hohhot, Inner Mongolia's capital, to destinations in Xinjiang and Kazakhstan by over 800 km.", 'node_id': '022c2bf5-8140-4f36-8316-d238a2ce404a', 'score': 1.213369369506836}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 0.6532168835401535, 'vram_usage': 1.29443359375}
