 51%|█████     | 253/500 [41:47<26:54,  6.54s/it]['Scott Sidney'] {'response': "The provided context is insufficient regarding Scott Sidney's career length to compare it with Alain Resnais's career. However, it does state that Alain Resnais's career extended over more than six decades, but no information is provided about Scott Sidney.", 'query': 'Which director had the longest career, Alain Resnais or Scott Sidney?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Alain Resnais (] ; 3 June 19221 March 2014) was a French film director and screenwriter whose career extended over more than six decades. After training as a film editor in the mid-1940s, he went on to direct a number of short films which included "Night and Fog" (1955), an influential documentary about the Nazi concentration camps.', 'node_id': 'aa2a40ef-cd94-4498-b464-a5bfe600af21', 'score': 1.03244149684906}, {'text': 'The movie won the Academy Award for Best Writing, Story and Screenplay - Written Directly for the Screen; Mastroianni was nominated for Best Actor in a Leading Role (Marcello Mastroianni) and Germi for Best Director.', 'node_id': 'b8fce84d-269e-4dab-823b-ddf949ff9172', 'score': 1.170116662979126}, {'text': 'Giovanni Fusco (10 October 1906, Sant\'Agata dei Goti, Benevento – 31 May 1968, Rome) was an Italian composer, pianist and conductor, who has written numerous film scores since 1936, including those of Alain Resnais\'s "Hiroshima mon amour" (1959) and "La guerre est finie" (1966), as well as of most of the 1948-1964 films directed by Michelangelo Antonioni, from "N.U."', 'node_id': '97b62bd2-316c-4281-88bf-855441c3af92', 'score': 1.1756608486175537}, {'text': 'Life of Riley (French: Aimer, boire et chanter ) is a 2014 French comedy-drama film directed by Alain Resnais in his final feature film before his death. Adapted from the play "Life of Riley" by Alan Ayckbourn, the film had its premiere in the competition section of the 64th Berlin International Film Festival, just three weeks before Resnais died, where it won the Alfred Bauer Prize.', 'node_id': 'd4a0f6db-070e-4188-94a9-3cae1bab328c', 'score': 1.1897252798080444}, {'text': 'Jokūbas Bernardas Šernas (30 July 1925 – 3 July 2015), commonly known as Jacques Sernas and sometimes credited as Jack Sernas, was a Lithuanian-born French actor with an international film career.', 'node_id': '10c8c3d0-50b0-4cd0-8a86-4834569ee071', 'score': 1.2267459630966187}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'CONTRADICTION'}, 'latency': 1.0807895176112652, 'vram_usage': 1.18896484375}
