['Scott Sidney'] {'response': "The provided context is insufficient regarding Scott Sidney's career length to make a comparison with Alain Resnais. However, it does state that Alain Resnais had a career that extended over more than six decades, but there is no information provided about Scott Sidney's career duration. Therefore, I cannot determine which director had the longest career based on the given context.", 'query': 'Which director had the longest career, Alain Resnais or Scott Sidney?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Alain Resnais (] ; 3 June 19221 March 2014) was a French film director and screenwriter whose career extended over more than six decades. After training as a film editor in the mid-1940s, he went on to direct a number of short films which included "Night and Fog" (1955), an influential documentary about the Nazi concentration camps.', 'node_id': 'aa2a40ef-cd94-4498-b464-a5bfe600af21', 'score': 8.951045036315918}, {'text': "L'Année dernière à Marienbad (released in the US as Last Year at Marienbad and in the UK as Last Year in Marienbad) is a 1961 French-Italian film directed by Alain Resnais from a screenplay by Alain Robbe-Grillet.", 'node_id': '103a79c4-6593-4328-b03f-a54d5377b515', 'score': 7.577496528625488}, {'text': 'Life of Riley (French: Aimer, boire et chanter ) is a 2014 French comedy-drama film directed by Alain Resnais in his final feature film before his death. Adapted from the play "Life of Riley" by Alan Ayckbourn, the film had its premiere in the competition section of the 64th Berlin International Film Festival, just three weeks before Resnais died, where it won the Alfred Bauer Prize.', 'node_id': 'd4a0f6db-070e-4188-94a9-3cae1bab328c', 'score': 6.895841121673584}, {'text': 'Marker is often associated with the Left Bank Cinema movement that occurred in the late 1950s and included such other filmmakers as Alain Resnais, Agnès Varda, Henri Colpi and Armand Gatti.', 'node_id': '59bac730-4f16-47c4-9a15-77a66ef3ea61', 'score': 6.745776176452637}, {'text': 'Muriel (French: Muriel ou le Temps d\'un retour , literally "Muriel, or the Time of a Return") is a 1963 French film directed by Alain Resnais. It was Resnais\'s third feature film, following "Hiroshima mon amour" (1959) and "L\'Année dernière à Marienbad" (1961), and in common with those films it explores the challenge of integrating a remembered or imagined past with the life of the present.', 'node_id': '3193dd33-2763-4b07-aff5-f5340279c827', 'score': 6.339463233947754}, {'text': 'Isle of Flowers (Portuguese: Ilha das Flores ) is a 1989 Brazilian short film by Jorge Furtado. It tracks the path of a tomato from garden to dump with the help of a monotone voiceover and a collection of bizarre images. While a very humorous film, the message it delivers about how human beings treat each other is anything but such. The director himself has stated that the film was inspired by the works of Kurt Vonnegut and Alain Resnais, among others.', 'node_id': '367bcbe6-5230-43b6-8c7b-5f51ab320de2', 'score': 6.0733256340026855}, {'text': 'Hiroshima mon amour (] , "Hiroshima My Love"; Japanese: 二十四時間の情事 "Nijūyojikan\'nojōji", "Twenty-four-hour affair") is a 1959 drama film directed by French film director Alain Resnais, with a screenplay by Marguerite Duras. It is the documentation of an intensely personal conversation between a French-Japanese couple about memory and forgetfulness. It was a major catalyst for the Left Bank Cinema, making highly innovative use of miniature flashbacks to create a uniquely nonlinear storyline.', 'node_id': 'f1d91061-a243-46b7-9f58-dafa4e8042b3', 'score': 6.014496803283691}, {'text': 'It also makes oblique reference to the controversial subject of the Algerian War, which had recently been brought to an end. "Muriel" was Resnais\'s second collaboration with Jean Cayrol, who had also written the screenplay of "Nuit et brouillard" ("Night and Fog") (1955).', 'node_id': '1a698a70-9fcc-4e48-bd8a-caf0b99d8921', 'score': 5.583090782165527}, {'text': 'Lawrence Sidney Eagleburger (August 1, 1930 – June 4, 2011) was an American statesman and career diplomat, who served briefly as the Secretary of State under President George H. W. Bush. Previously, he had served in lesser capacities under Presidents Richard Nixon, Jimmy Carter, and Ronald Reagan, and as Deputy Secretary of State under George H. W. Bush.', 'node_id': 'ccc39806-4590-4c67-933a-1c7fdef91d48', 'score': 5.55173397064209}, {'text': 'The War is Over (French: La Guerre est Finie -1966) is a French drama film about a leftist in Franco\'s Spain, directed by Alain Resnais and starring Yves Montand, Ingrid Thulin, and Geneviève Bujold. Joseph Losey directed a sequel, "Roads to the South" (French: "Les Routes du Sud" -1978).', 'node_id': '9891b7af-8db8-4d87-9dcd-e50223f134b1', 'score': 5.522573471069336}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 5.625162620097399, 'vram_usage': 0.0}
