 51%|█████     | 256/500 [42:35<45:56, 11.30s/it]['1945'] {'response': 'The provided context is insufficient regarding the specific year Roy Rogers and his third wife starred in a film directed by Frank McDonald. The context mentions several films directed by Frank McDonald that starred Roy Rogers, including "Song of Arizona" (1946) and "Rainbow Over Texas" (1946), but it does not specify the involvement of his third wife or the exact year of their collaboration.', 'query': 'What year did Roy Rogers and his third wife star in a film directed by Frank McDonald?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Frank McDonald (November 9, 1899 Baltimore, Maryland – March 8, 1980 Oxnard, California) was an American film and television director, active from 1935 to 1966. He directed more than 100 films, including many Westerns starring Gene Autry and Roy Rogers, and numerous TV show episodes. He is interred at Conejo Mountain Memorial Park in Camarillo, California.', 'node_id': '0e771a56-5610-4a8b-9e44-ef16a003832c', 'score': 0.6270731091499329}, {'text': 'Song of Arizona is a 1946 American Western film directed by Frank McDonald and starring Roy Rogers.', 'node_id': '9aafa0be-c7bc-468e-b638-788944e04e48', 'score': 0.9198951721191406}, {'text': 'San Fernando Valley is a 1944 American western film directed by John English and starring Roy Rogers, Dale Evans and Jean Porter. The film was part of the long-running series of Roy Rogers films produced by Republic Pictures.', 'node_id': '057b3508-fe02-4dee-b0e9-064fb350e492', 'score': 0.9760684967041016}, {'text': 'Rainbow Over Texas is a film from 1946 in which Roy Rogers plays himself as a famous cowboy-singer returning to Texas. Directed by Frank McDonald from a story by Max Brand, it co-stars George "Gabby" Hayes and Dale Evans.', 'node_id': 'b92d6c76-fd1e-4484-9efd-d5187b37438c', 'score': 1.0049479007720947}, {'text': 'Apache Rose is a 1947 American Trucolor Western film directed by William Witney and starring Roy Rogers. It was the first Roy Rogers Western shot in the process though most copies on DVD are in monochrome.', 'node_id': '0725130a-07af-47e3-a8ce-79b044a5533a', 'score': 1.0859334468841553}], 'consistency_check': 'CONSISTENT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 1.1983247827738523, 'vram_usage': 1.23583984375}
