['1945'] {'response': 'The provided context is insufficient regarding the specific year Roy Rogers and his third wife starred in a film directed by Frank McDonald. While it mentions that Frank McDonald directed films featuring Roy Rogers, it does not specify the year they starred together or the name of the film that included his third wife.', 'query': 'What year did Roy Rogers and his third wife star in a film directed by Frank McDonald?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Frank McDonald (November 9, 1899 Baltimore, Maryland – March 8, 1980 Oxnard, California) was an American film and television director, active from 1935 to 1966. He directed more than 100 films, including many Westerns starring Gene Autry and Roy Rogers, and numerous TV show episodes. He is interred at Conejo Mountain Memorial Park in Camarillo, California.', 'node_id': '0e771a56-5610-4a8b-9e44-ef16a003832c', 'score': 0.6270731091499329}, {'text': 'Song of Arizona is a 1946 American Western film directed by Frank McDonald and starring Roy Rogers.', 'node_id': '9aafa0be-c7bc-468e-b638-788944e04e48', 'score': 0.9198951721191406}, {'text': 'San Fernando Valley is a 1944 American western film directed by John English and starring Roy Rogers, Dale Evans and Jean Porter. The film was part of the long-running series of Roy Rogers films produced by Republic Pictures.', 'node_id': '057b3508-fe02-4dee-b0e9-064fb350e492', 'score': 0.9760684967041016}, {'text': 'Rainbow Over Texas is a film from 1946 in which Roy Rogers plays himself as a famous cowboy-singer returning to Texas. Directed by Frank McDonald from a story by Max Brand, it co-stars George "Gabby" Hayes and Dale Evans.', 'node_id': 'b92d6c76-fd1e-4484-9efd-d5187b37438c', 'score': 1.0049479007720947}, {'text': 'Apache Rose is a 1947 American Trucolor Western film directed by William Witney and starring Roy Rogers. It was the first Roy Rogers Western shot in the process though most copies on DVD are in monochrome.', 'node_id': '0725130a-07af-47e3-a8ce-79b044a5533a', 'score': 1.0859334468841553}, {'text': 'More recently, Roy played the part of Mr Hill in "Pride & Prejudice" (2005), and Gaffer Tom in "Robin Hood" (2010).', 'node_id': '4f202abd-3f96-4788-9d23-91169c3e4668', 'score': 1.0909640789031982}, {'text': 'Gary Ross directed the first film, while Francis Lawrence directed the next three films.', 'node_id': 'bfa49cd3-4460-4dac-a409-39122d86ed10', 'score': 1.116938829421997}, {'text': '"Roy\'s Wedding" is the second episode of the ninth season of the American comedy television series "The Office" and the show\'s 178th episode overall. The episode originally aired on NBC on September 27, 2012. The episode guest stars David Denman as Roy Anderson, Michael Patrick McGill as his brother Kenny, Robert R. Shafer as Bob Vance, and Ameenah Kaplan as Val.', 'node_id': '2fed4a45-4919-475d-babd-e72f99e84a18', 'score': 1.1321686506271362}, {'text': "The Pastor's Wife is a 2011 biographical television film, starring Rose McGowan as Mary Winkler and based on the true crime book of the same title by author Diane Fanning. It premiered on Saturday, November 5, at 8 pm ET/PT on the Lifetime Network.", 'node_id': 'eeeecfb9-2319-446b-b21a-a52183172b44', 'score': 1.1360814571380615}, {'text': 'William Fichtner, Barry Pepper, Ruth Wilson, James Badge Dale, Tom Wilkinson and Helena Bonham Carter also are featured in supporting roles. It is the first theatrical film featuring the Lone Ranger and Tonto characters in more than 32 years.', 'node_id': '21d4b1ce-0571-4613-9d57-8718a343efe5', 'score': 1.1426020860671997}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 0.8840396534651518, 'vram_usage': 1.23583984375}
