the downtown along the Paulista Avenue and in the neighborhood of Brooklin. At one time, the city was home to the tallest building in Latin America, the Martinelli Building, which opened in 1929 at a height of 130 meters.", 'node_id': 'cd502668-a689-45ef-9d0d-2e7b907cb9eb', 'score': 1.1553301811218262}, {'text': 'Hanggin Rear Banner (Mongolian: ᠬᠠᠩᠭᠢᠨ ᠬᠣᠶᠢᠲᠤ ᠬᠣᠰᠢᠭᠤ Қанин Қоыиту қосиу "Qaŋɣin Qoyitu qosiɣu"; ), 1,767\xa0km², 300,000 inhabitants (2004),', 'node_id': 'f3a47e1c-0340-4955-9f4b-fc730a3e2b68', 'score': 1.1704078912734985}, {'text': 'Republic Plaza (Chinese: 共和大厦) is one of the three tallest skyscrapers in Singapore, located at the Southern end of Raffles Place in the Downtown Core, the central business district of Singapore. It shares the title of "tallest building" with the OUB Centre and UOB Plaza One. Built at 280 metres (919 feet) tall, it was completed in 1995, and incorporates earthquake proof features despite the city being relatively far from earthquake zones.', 'node_id': 'e4a9db01-ed30-4b9b-bcbf-6ce7233a4d07', 'score': 1.1729193925857544}, {'text': '767\xa0km², 300,000 inhabitants (2004), administrative center: Shanba (陕坝镇).', 'node_id': 'eab67357-3f68-48e3-9d6b-67b3315ab8b6', 'score': 1.1740291118621826}, {'text': 'and Xilin Gol to the north. It is under the administration of Ulaan Chab City, which lies to the south along the G55 Erenhot–Guangzhou Expressway. The most important settlement in the banner is Baiyinchagan.', 'node_id': '1adc3f19-e343-4775-b2b9-23f94e0f58d6', 'score': 1.1869617700576782}, {'text': 'The city halls or offices of the province governors are called "sala wa kan" (ศาลาว่าการ, literally meaning "government pavilion") or "sala klang changwat" (ศาลากลางจังหวัด, literally meaning a provincial main pavilion).', 'node_id': '8d6bd166-057c-47fe-97a0-6050b2dbc542', 'score': 1.1988036632537842}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 3.836858930066228, 'vram_usage': 1.16552734375}
