xt': 'Jack and his Comrades is a short Irish fairy tale describing the title character\'s story of success with the help of his animal helpers, collected by folklorist Patrick Kennedy from a resident of County Wexford, Ireland, and published in "Legendary Fictions of the Irish Celts" (1866). It was later reprinted, revised but only slightly, by Joseph Jacobs in his Celtic fairy tale compilation.', 'node_id': 'b5bc2a2c-a3af-4e0f-be8f-189061c6b7bd', 'score': 0.8648111820220947}, {'text': 'Brian Edward Patrick Kennedy (born 12 October 1966, Belfast, Northern Ireland) is an Irish singer-songwriter and author, who is known for his ballads, and has represented Ireland in the Eurovision Song Contest 2006. He is the younger brother of the late musician Bap Kennedy.', 'node_id': '5d274b29-a32f-4050-abe7-2c590be95d98', 'score': 0.8703716993331909}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'ENTAILMENT', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 0.8310273345559835, 'vram_usage': 1.28271484375}
