['3,384,569'] {'response': 'The population of Addis Ababa, the city in which the National Archives and Library of Ethiopia is located, is 3,384,569 according to the 2007 population census. Addis Ababa is the capital and largest city of Ethiopia, and it has an annual growth rate of 3.8%.', 'query': 'What is the population according to the 2007 population census of the city in which the National Archives and Library of Ethiopia is located?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': "This is a list of ethnic groups in Ethiopia that are officially recognized by the government. It is a list taken from the 2007 Ethiopian National Census: Population size and percentage of Ethiopia's total population according to the 1994 and 2007 censuses follows each entry.", 'node_id': 'd33a6782-ab18-4a73-a5ce-a13f76090c77', 'score': 17.197708129882812}, {'text': 'The National Archives and Library of Ethiopia, located in Addis Ababa, is the national library and archives of the country. The library was inaugurated in 1944 by Emperor Haile Selassie and began service with books donated by the emperor.', 'node_id': '12c749ad-e7d9-4f31-805b-d8f3205fcb78', 'score': 14.163277626037598}, {'text': 'Addis Ababa (Amharic: አዲስ አበባ "Addis Abäba " ] , "new flower"; Oromo: "Finfinne" , ] "Natural Spring(s)") or Addis Abeba (the spelling used by the official Ethiopian Mapping Authority), is the capital and largest city of Ethiopia. It has a population of 3,384,569 according to the 2007 population census, with annual growth rate of 3.8%.', 'node_id': 'a50979b5-6abc-445d-9e94-f34b148e32af', 'score': 13.54649543762207}, {'text': "Orlinda is a city in Robertson County, Tennessee. The population was 594 at the 2000 census, at which time it was a town; the community became a city in February 2001. The City of Orlinda conducted its own, independent census 2007. The results of that census were submitted to the State of Tennessee which conducted a review and random sample before officially certifying the results, which it did in May, 2007. The 2010 U.S. Census results list Orlinda's current population at 859.", 'node_id': 'da747605-6f82-4680-b57c-8425b4f1f5f2', 'score': 12.076652526855469}, {'text': 'Tiruchirappalli is a city in the Indian state of Tamil Nadu. It is the fourth most populous city and is the densest regional urban area in the state. According to the 2001 census, Tiruchirappalli had a population of 752,066 with in the city limits and an extended urban agglomeration population of 866,354. According to the 2011 provisional population totals, the city has a population of 846,915 while the regional urban area has 1,021,717 residents.', 'node_id': '3a7a5ac3-7b8b-4dc9-a7b2-c336622ec9b4', 'score': 11.723477363586426}, {'text': 'The National Archives of Zambia preserves the archives of the Republic of Zambia and maintains its legal deposit library. The library holds 70,000 volumes. Its headquarters is located in Ridgeway in the city of Lusaka.', 'node_id': '12620246-e2c6-400c-a5da-c93adb42263f', 'score': 11.618606567382812}, {'text': 'Gaboš (Serbian Cyrillic: ) is a village in Vukovar-Srijem County, Croatia. There are 613 inhabitants, the majority of the population which are Serbs, who make up 95% of the population according to the 2001 population census.', 'node_id': 'ec77b2b2-d43d-47cf-bb0f-abe7334763d5', 'score': 11.230527877807617}, {'text': 'Kirton is a village in Nottinghamshire, England. It is located 3 mi east of Ollerton. According to the United Kingdom Census 2001 it had a population of 273, reducing to 261 at the 2011 census.', 'node_id': 'ecc343bb-d28b-40f0-a9ce-15b2c6ea84a5', 'score': 10.802589416503906}, {'text': "According to the adjusted 2001 census figures, Bangladesh's population stood at 129.3 million (an initial count put it at 124.4 million; an adjustment for the standard rate of undercounting then boosted the figure). According to the census, Hindus were 9.2 per cent of the population.", 'node_id': '14239b08-f5d6-4d26-b7ba-2b913946140b', 'score': 10.592647552490234}, {'text': 'Biratnagar (Devanāgarī: विराटनगर) is a metropolitan city of Nepal. According to the 2011 census, the city ranks fourth in population. It ranks second in population density after Kathmandu. Biratnagar is the industrial capital of Nepal and has a total area of 40.108\xa0mi² (103.88\xa0km²).', 'node_id': 'a7be9c22-3b21-42d8-8460-52c055698cac', 'score': 10.437106132507324}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'ENTAILMENT', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 0.7798841781914234, 'vram_usage': 0.0}
