['The Dragon School in Oxford'] {'response': "The provided context is insufficient regarding Ian Harland's educational background prior to studying at the oldest college at the University of Cambridge.", 'query': 'Where did Ian Harland study prior to studying at the oldest college at the University of Cambridge?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Wolfson College is a constituent college of the University of Cambridge in Cambridge, England. The majority of students at the college are postgraduates. The college also admits "mature" undergraduates (aged 21 and above), with around 15% of students studying undergraduate degree courses at the university. The college was founded in 1965 as "University College", and changed its name to Wolfson College in 1973 in recognition of the benefaction of the Wolfson Foundation. Wolfson is located to the west of Cambridge city centre, near the University Library.', 'node_id': 'dea6a5d7-ee6d-483d-a5a9-be5a7fc0fa89', 'score': 11.87356948852539}, {'text': 'Vaughan Hart is a leading architectural historian, and Professor of Architecture in the Department of Architecture and Civil Engineering at the University of Bath. Hart studied architecture at Bath and Cambridge Universities (Trinity Hall), where he was taught by Michael Brawne, Patrick Hodgkinson, Peter Smithson and Dalibor Vesely. He worked first as an architectural assistant to Colin St John Wilson on the British Library project in London, before studying for a doctorate in Cambridge on Inigo Jones under Joseph Rykwert.', 'node_id': '3ecc3aa0-0153-429c-b09c-ad4a2c74e11f', 'score': 10.421541213989258}, {'text': 'Although Oxford University and Cambridge University offer both pre-clinical and clinical courses in medicine, students who study pre-clinical medicine at one of these universities may move to another university for clinical studies. At other universities students stay at the same university for both pre-clinical and clinical work.', 'node_id': '304423d4-b80e-408c-8285-b8b193dc37e0', 'score': 10.135992050170898}, {'text': 'Trinity Hall Boat Club (THBC) is the rowing club of Trinity Hall, a college of the University of Cambridge. Founded in 1827 it is amongst the oldest college boat clubs in Cambridge, England. Historically, it is the most successful Cambridge college at Henley Royal Regatta with a number of wins, including winning all the events but one in 1887.', 'node_id': '9264c31d-9e0f-470b-b7fe-dedd0cae7d37', 'score': 9.926002502441406}, {'text': 'Joshua D. Zimmerman (born 1966) is Professor of History at Yeshiva University, where he holds the Eli and Diana Zborowski Professorial Chair in Interdisciplinary Holocaust Studies. He is the author of "The Polish Underground and the Jews, 1939-1945" by Cambridge University Press (2015, hardback) and of "Contested Memories.', 'node_id': '37e2682a-62fe-4baa-a81d-40dc92ae1bfa', 'score': 9.759100914001465}, {'text': "One of ten children, Boykin grew up in Greenville, South Carolina. He started studies in Opera Performance at South Carolina State College before transferring to the North Carolina School of the Arts. He left NCSA in 1990 and moved to the Hartt School of the University of Hartford where he received his Bachelor of Music in Vocal Performance in 1995. He later studied toward a Master's degree in Opera and Jazz Vocals from Howard University.", 'node_id': 'dd28be82-6feb-4412-a3b7-49240960233a', 'score': 8.439980506896973}, {'text': 'Peterhouse is a constituent college of the University of Cambridge, England. It is the oldest college of the university, having been founded in 1284 by Hugo de Balsham, Bishop of Ely, and granted its charter by King Edward I. Today, Peterhouse has 226 undergraduates, 86 full-time graduate students and 45 fellows. The modern name of Peterhouse does not include the word "college".', 'node_id': 'e923644f-1ad6-4f76-a922-ab7a1a8f0e66', 'score': 8.39522647857666}, {'text': "The College of Arts and Sciences of Ohio University is one of eleven colleges at Ohio University, centrally located in Wilson Hall on the College Green in Athens, Ohio. The college is often referred to as Ohio University's oldest college, but that reference is not entirely precise. Whether or not the college can claim to be the university's oldest, it does remain at the institution's core. The college currently features eighteen organized academic departments.", 'node_id': 'fc8da7ea-e5ad-459d-8776-756d08e58020', 'score': 7.625190734863281}, {'text': "News in Environmental/Environmental Health. In environmental disciplines, QS World Rankings recognizes the University of California, Berkeley, as the world's leading university in Environmental Studies with 100 points in Academic Reputation. U.S. News also ranks it as the best global university for environment and ecology. A study of AJAE authors and their university affiliations found it to have the highest number of pages per research faculty member.", 'node_id': '7ca0f6d0-cda6-40e4-91d1-0015a56f894c', 'score': 6.974703788757324}, {'text': 'The College of Charleston (also known as CofC, The College, or simply, Charleston) is a public sea-grant and space-grant university located in historic downtown Charleston, South Carolina, United States. Founded in 1770 and chartered in 1785, it is the oldest college in South Carolina, the 13th oldest institution of higher learning in the United States, and the oldest municipal college in the country.', 'node_id': 'd7af607f-f60a-44c9-b85a-537c65af9796', 'score': 6.956879138946533}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'ENTAILMENT', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 0.6780836023390293, 'vram_usage': 0.0}
