trons in which 70%+ of total revenue is derived from sales of food. After a vote in late 2015; Oldham county has become a completely wet county.", 'node_id': '84135df2-366c-4acb-a354-c5e099c5d227', 'score': 1.063342571258545}, {'text': 'Casey County is a county located in the U.S. Commonwealth of Kentucky. As of the 2010 census, the population was 15,955. Its county seat is Liberty. The county was formed in 1806 from the western part of Lincoln County and named for Colonel William Casey, a pioneer settler who moved his family to Kentucky in 1779. It is the only Kentucky county entirely in the Knobs region. Casey County is home to annual Casey County Apple Festival, and is a prohibition or dry county. It is considered part of the Appalachian region of Kentucky.', 'node_id': '1ef1503f-b26f-4f0c-9afa-bcb73a9b2f82', 'score': 1.1009994745254517}, {'text': 'Shawnee State Fishing Lake is approximately eight miles northwest of Topeka, Kansas, and is in northern Shawnee County, Kansas. This lake is sometimes confused with Lake Shawnee, on the east side of Topeka. It is a 135 acre surface area lake with a maximum depth of 25 ft . This is a manmade freshwater lake, which was constructed in the late 1960s. The lake is widest at the dam, which is at the south end of the lake. It can be reached by a number of roads.', 'node_id': '1ae8f93a-d221-44a0-b308-44a767946d8c', 'score': 1.1433467864990234}, {'text': 'Lakeland is a city in Shelby County, Tennessee, and a suburb of Memphis. The population was 12,430 at the 2010 census.', 'node_id': '8be1e49f-458d-4fa2-a432-2c8edc6df125', 'score': 1.1630717515945435}, {'text': 'Wheeling Island is the most populated island in the Ohio River. It lies within the city of Wheeling in Ohio County, West Virginia, in the United States. The 2000 census showed a resident population of 3,142 people on the island, which has a land area of 1.514\xa0km² (374 acres). Neville Island, PA is larger (3.4\xa0km²) but has fewer people (1,232).', 'node_id': '3cc8f901-6b5d-481f-b99b-9d3357d0de4d', 'score': 1.1658235788345337}, {'text': "Osage State Fishing Lake is located in northern Osage County, Kansas. It is a mile east of US 75. Scranton, Kansas, is to the lake's northwest and Overbrook, Kansas, is to the northeast. Osage Lake is a freshwater man-made lake, constructed in 1955. It has a surface area of 140 acres, The parkland in which the lake is contained has 366 acreas of land, mostly tall grass prairie with numerous wooded areas. The lake is owned by the State of Kansas.", 'node_id': '598f5324-da1f-44bc-9b82-dc4916ccd8af', 'score': 1.1870285272598267}, {'text': "Kentucky Oaks Mall is an enclosed super-regional shopping mall in Paducah, Kentucky, USA. Managed by Cafaro Company, the mall includes more than 90 inline stores, as well as regional radio station Rock 98.3 WJLI. Its anchor stores comprise JCPenney, Best Buy, Elder-Beerman, a Dillard's store divided into two sub-stores, and Dick's Sporting Goods. It was the largest mall in Kentucky by gross leasable area when it opened, and remains the state's third-largest, behind Fayette Mall in Lexington and Mall St. Matthews in Louisville.", 'node_id': '1c0de7d4-854f-43eb-8307-741ee97d8f89', 'score': 1.226984977722168}, {'text': 'Greater Newport Rural Historic District is a national historic district located near Newport, Giles County, Virginia. It encompasses a total of 737 contributing buildings and 25 contributing structures in the rural area near the village of Newport. It encompasses the previously listed Newport Historic District. The district includes primarily 19th- and early-20th-century farmsteads and complexes. Notable buildings include the "Camper" Cabin (late 18th century), Albert Meredith Cabin (c. 1840), E. L. Lucas House (c.', 'node_id': '12f565d9-d259-4ae5-bfea-a3ed9d5e5a52', 'score': 1.230231761932373}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 1.4117250684648752, 'vram_usage': 1.24755859375}
