 64%|██████▍   | 320/500 [51:57<41:36, 13.87s/it]['Serri'] {'response': 'The provided context is insufficient regarding an individual named Serri. However, it does mention John Fogerty, who was an architect and engineer, but there is no indication that he was an actor. Therefore, the answer to the question is that John Fogerty was not an actor, and the context does not provide information about Serri being an actor either.', 'query': 'Who was also an actor, Serri or John Fogerty?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'John Fogerty was an Irish millwright, architect, builder, and civil engineer, active in early to mid-19th-century Limerick.He was the brother of Joseph Fogerty, Sr. and the father of engineer and novelist Joseph Fogerty of London, architect William Fogerty of Dublin, and grandfather of architect John Frederick Fogerty. He retired as an architect sometime between 1870 and 1879.', 'node_id': '338319eb-8aa4-4bd9-8362-5c883bcff8c0', 'score': 0.9150598049163818}, {'text': 'Joseph Fogerty Sr. was an Irish builder and architect active in nineteenth-century Limerick. Born in Limerick into a family of builders, he was the father of Robert Fogerty and George J. Fogerty; brother of John Fogerty (engineer), uncle of engineer and novelist Joseph Fogerty of London and architect William Fogerty of Dublin, and great uncle of architect John Frederick Fogerty. He designed and built the Theatre Royal, Limerick, Henry Street. From the 1870s until his death, he was partners with his son Robert in the firm Joseph Fogerty & Son.', 'node_id': '447e8e76-d162-4bc7-bd79-f37bc09758fc', 'score': 1.0094959735870361}, {'text': 'Jokūbas Bernardas Šernas (30 July 1925 – 3 July 2015), commonly known as Jacques Sernas and sometimes credited as Jack Sernas, was a Lithuanian-born French actor with an international film career.', 'node_id': '10c8c3d0-50b0-4cd0-8a86-4834569ee071', 'score': 1.0325322151184082}, {'text': 'John Arthur Lithgow ( ; born October 19 , 1945) is an American actor, musician, singer, comedian, voice actor, and author. He has received two Tony Awards, six Emmy Awards, two Golden Globe Awards, three Screen Actors Guild Awards, an American Comedy Award, four Drama Desk Awards and has also been nominated for two Academy Awards and four Grammy Awards. Lithgow has received a star on the Hollywood Walk of Fame and has been inducted into the American Theater Hall of Fame.', 'node_id': 'ba0b4356-29a6-45b0-8eb3-e02108aac30a', 'score': 1.0405704975128174}, {'text': 'John Frederick Fogerty {\'1\': ", \'2\': ", \'3\': \'ARIBA\', \'4\': "} (1863–1938), was an Irish architect and engineer active in mid- to late-19th-century Limerick, London, Shropshire, Bournemouth, Pretoria, and Zambia. Born in Limerick, he was the son of architect William Fogerty, grandson of architect and engineer John Fogerty (engineer), and nephew of engineer and novelist Joseph Fogerty.', 'node_id': '5f7900a1-b49e-4bf2-bc31-d0a76a9887f1', 'score': 1.0501238107681274}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 1.0287619158625603, 'vram_usage': 1.17724609375}
