 64%|██████▍   | 321/500 [52:15<44:47, 15.01s/it]['international football competition'] {'response': "The international football competition for women that Liu Ailing played in the 1991, 1995, and 1999 editions is the FIFA Women's World Cup. This competition is contested by the senior women's national teams of the members of the Fédération Internationale de Football Association (FIFA), and it has been held every four years since its inaugural tournament in 1991, which took place in China. Liu Ailing represented the China national team in these tournaments, showcasing her skills as a playmaking midfielder on the international stage.", 'query': 'What is the international football competition for women that Liu Ailing played in the 1991,1995, 1999 editions?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': "Liu Ailing (; born June 2, 1967) is a Chinese former footballer who played for the China national team at the 1991, 1995 and 1999 editions of the FIFA Women's World Cup. She won a silver medal at the 1996 Atlanta Olympics and participated at the 2000 Sydney Olympics. A playmaking midfielder, she played professional club football in Japan and the United States.", 'node_id': 'e451d6c8-9849-4f87-a59d-9a183f4e3702', 'score': 0.4115435481071472}, {'text': "EAFF E-1 Football Championship is an international football competition in East Asia for national teams of the East Asian Football Federation (EAFF). The competition between women's national teams is held alongside men's competition.", 'node_id': 'f75e12ae-725f-4e54-8ce1-7e255b60ee2c', 'score': 0.915002167224884}, {'text': "EAFF E-1 Football Championship, known as the East Asian Football Championship from 2003 to 2010, and the EAFF East Asian Cup for the 2013 and 2015 editions, is a men's international football competition in East Asia for member nations of the East Asian Football Federation (EAFF). Before the EAFF was founded in 2002, the Dynasty Cup was held between the East Asian top four teams, and was regarded as the unofficial East Asian Championship. There is a separate competition for both men (first held in 2003) and women (first held in 2005).", 'node_id': '497c7485-7f57-45a6-b8ab-9330a6ff66f6', 'score': 1.0046813488006592}, {'text': 'The FIFA Women\'s World Cup is an international football competition contested by the senior women\'s national teams of the members of "Fédération Internationale de Football Association" (FIFA), the sport\'s global governing body. The competition has been held every four years since 1991, when the inaugural tournament, then called the Women\'s World Championship, was held in China.', 'node_id': '70b2117c-2fd7-42dd-967b-4f1ab955bd94', 'score': 1.0187456607818604}, {'text': "There was also a combined points competition in 2005, where the results of the men's and women's teams are added together (not including qualifiers).", 'node_id': '3e10824c-d037-4043-b7e0-b2e2df8c600a', 'score': 1.0553269386291504}], 'consistency_check': 'CONFLICT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'ENTAILMENT', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 1.2981610223650932, 'vram_usage': 1.28271484375}
