['Spring city'] {'response': 'The city that contains the Yunnan Provincial Museum is Kunming, which is also known by the nickname "Spring City." This nickname is attributed to its pleasant weather throughout the year. Kunming serves as the capital of Yunnan Province and is recognized as the political, economic, communications, and cultural center of the province.', 'query': 'The city that contains the Yunnan Provincial Museum is also known by what nickname?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': "Yunnan Provincial Museum () is located in Kunming, on Guangfu Road. It houses an exhibition centered on Yunnan's ethnic minorities, as well as a collection of artifacts from tomb excavations at Jinning on the southern rim of Lake Dian.", 'node_id': '51f9f21a-e48b-4fa5-b644-5b3dad909141', 'score': 0.49043262004852295}, {'text': 'Kunming City Museum (昆明市博物馆) is a history museum in Kunming City, Yunnan, China. Smaller than the Yunnan Provincial Museum, Its most notable exhibit is about the history of the city. Other features include a dinosaur exhibit and a rotating exhibition space that holds anything from history to art exhibitions.', 'node_id': '6b839937-f9fa-4a89-a90a-57c75c18fdd6', 'score': 0.6643844842910767}, {'text': 'Kunming ( ; ) is the capital of and largest city in Yunnan Province, Southwest China. Known as Yunnan-Fu (云南府 , "Yúnnánfǔ") until the 1920s, today it is a prefecture-level city and the political, economic, communications and cultural centre of the province as well as the seat of the provincial government. Kunming is also called the Spring city due to its weather. The headquarters of many of Yunnan\'s large businesses are in Kunming.', 'node_id': '4fa98c9f-c4b8-40f4-aeb8-8adc0366c66c', 'score': 0.780792236328125}, {'text': 'Her body and belongings are currently under the care of the Hunan Provincial Museum, which has allowed occasional international exhibits.', 'node_id': '2ddd7ea6-38f1-421c-bd71-251edf0c4cb9', 'score': 0.9055821299552917}, {'text': 'Dianchi Lake (Chinese:\xa0滇池 , "Diānchí"), also known as Lake Dian and Kunming Lake (昆明湖 , "Kūnmínghú"), is a large lake located on the Yunnan-Guizhou Plateau close to Kunming, Yunnan, in southern China. Its nickname is the "Sparkling Pearl Embedded in a Highland" and it was the model for the Kunming Lake in the Summer Palace in Beijing. Its name is the source of Yunnan\'s Chinese abbreviation 滇 .', 'node_id': '89762581-29da-4519-b2df-d9cba226f4d6', 'score': 1.0709247589111328}, {'text': "Qinyang () is a county-level city in Henan province, People's Republic of China. It is administered by the prefecture-level city Jiaozuo. The current population of Qinyang is estimated at 470,000. In 1999, the population stood at 444,480.", 'node_id': '06bcf2a9-9ada-4a8c-92c0-caa89f0c41a5', 'score': 1.0828173160552979}, {'text': 'Luang Namtha Museum, also Louang Namtha Provincial Museum, is a museum in Luang Namtha, Laos. Largely an anthropological museum, it contains numerous items related to local people such as ethnic clothing, Khamu bronze drums, textiles, ceramics, tools, household utensils, hand-crafted weapons, and Buddhism-related items.', 'node_id': 'f8dd3561-6250-479b-ad62-0207ad37bbc9', 'score': 1.0840264558792114}, {'text': "Tongcheng () is a subdistrict of the city of Fuding, Fujian, People's Republic of China.", 'node_id': 'fedfa726-8763-421a-85f4-058d7c795f1d', 'score': 1.0875921249389648}, {'text': 'The Zuiweng Pavilion (, is a pavilion lying to the south east of Chuzhou City, Anhui Province, People\'s Republic of China. Located in The Northern Song Dynasty whilst the structure that exists today dates to the Qing Dynasty (1644–1911). The pavilion takes its name from the Northern Song poet Ouyang Xiu, who called himself the "Old Toper" and wrote a poem entitled "Zuiweng Tingji" or "An Account of the Old Toper\'s Pavilion".', 'node_id': '86d305bc-3329-42f7-821f-ec30976f8499', 'score': 1.1283073425292969}, {'text': 'Yangzonghai Lake () (given on some maps as Yangzong Sea, though it is fresh water) is located between Yiliang County, Chenggong District and Chengjiang County, 45 kilometers east of Kunming City in Yunnan Province, China. About 30,000 people rely on the Lake as their drinking water. Yangzonghai Lake is noted for its underwater springs and is one of several scenic areas in Yunnan province, which is known for its biodiversity.', 'node_id': '43c908e5-b2d9-4ef0-86d8-76870ab87e71', 'score': 1.1400223970413208}, {'text': 'Shengjing Bank (in ) is a commercial bank, with its headquarters in Shenyang, Liaoning Province, China. It was established in 1996 as Shenyang City Commercial Bank and opened in Shenyang City only. It changed its name to Shengjing Bank in 2007 and has since opened a branch in Beijing, Tianjin, Dalian, Yingkou, Huludao, Shanghai, Anshan, Changchun, Benxi, Panjin, Chaoyang, Fushun, Jinzhou, Fuxin, Dandong and Liaoyang.', 'node_id': '4a840444-b1c3-4cae-a4a1-420779194948', 'score': 1.1430978775024414}, {'text': 'Sinopieris is a genus of butterflies in the family Pieridae. The genus occurs in Nepal, Tibet, Yunnan, Gansu, Shaanxi and Sichuan. All six species were originally included in "Pieris". The two genera are distinguished by the venation in the apical area of the forewing.', 'node_id': 'e8510cc4-c092-4998-afa2-e3451888ee64', 'score': 1.1701716184616089}, {'text': 'The city halls or offices of the province governors are called "sala wa kan" (ศาลาว่าการ, literally meaning "government pavilion") or "sala klang changwat" (ศาลากลางจังหวัด, literally meaning a provincial main pavilion).', 'node_id': '8d6bd166-057c-47fe-97a0-6050b2dbc542', 'score': 1.1740481853485107}, {'text': "Xiapu (; Foochow Romanized: Hà-puō) is a county in the municipal region of Ningde, Fujian, People's Republic of China, located along a stretch of East China Sea coast, with many harbours and islands. It is bordered by Fuding City and Zherong County to the north, Fu'an City and Ningde's urban area to the west, and—in Fuzhou City—Luoyuan County to the south.", 'node_id': 'c27105dd-6d01-40e5-b821-76681e2b0864', 'score': 1.1775470972061157}, {'text': 'The Wolong Special Administrative Region () is an area in Sichuan, China. It is located in the southwest of Wenchuan County, Ngawa Tibetan and Qiang Autonomous Prefecture of Sichuan. It was formerly known as Wolong Special Administrative Region of Wenchuan County, Sichuan Province and was founded in March 1983 with approval of the State Council. It was given its current name and placed under Sichuan provincial government with administrative supervision by the provincial department of forestry.', 'node_id': 'bdcce447-7b9a-454a-8d27-d6348622feaf', 'score': 1.200784683227539}, {'text': 'Yandu District () is one of three districts of Yancheng, Jiangsu province, China. (The other two are Tinghu District and Dafeng District).', 'node_id': 'a71452ee-56ac-4a1a-8bbe-1ccff796a913', 'score': 1.2012994289398193}, {'text': 'The Pearl River, also known by its Chinese name Zhujiang and formerly often known as the Canton River , is an extensive river system in southern China. The name "Pearl River" is also often used as a catch-all for the watersheds of the Xi ("West"), Bei ("North"), and Dong ("East") rivers of Guangdong. These rivers are all considered tributaries of the Pearl River because they share a common delta, the Pearl River Delta.', 'node_id': '20c80152-8c0a-4463-8ccd-baa40c825e99', 'score': 1.2025936841964722}, {'text': 'The Zhukaigou culture was a late Neolithic and early Bronze Age culture centered in the Ordos Plateau of Inner Mongolia, China. The type site at Zhukaigou was discovered in Ejin Horo Banner, Inner Mongolia, and excavated from 1977 to 1984. Zhukaigou culture is a reputed progenitor of the Ordos bronze culture and accordingly a first "Northern Zone" culture, extending to northern and central Inner Mongolia, northern Shaanxi, and northern Shanxi, with the Ordos region at its center.', 'node_id': '8f972e92-8d73-476f-a680-59d855abe755', 'score': 1.2042875289916992}, {'text': "The lake is a popular resort destination for people living in the nearby provincial capital of Kunming, which itself borders Dianchi Lake, one of China's biggest freshwater lakes but also one of its most polluted.", 'node_id': '80a0ade6-0086-4f96-9a34-67ff94c07b7e', 'score': 1.2278285026550293}, {'text': 'Shuangmiao () is a town under the administration of Hanggin Rear Banner in southwestern Inner Mongolia, China, located about 26 km southwest of the banner seat and 44 km north-northwest of downtown Bayannur. , it has 14 villages under its administration.', 'node_id': '89e54d1d-ad32-40e0-85df-fc6d547f5b82', 'score': 1.2322719097137451}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'ENTAILMENT', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 1.1209289859980345, 'vram_usage': 1.20068359375}
