['Aqua'] {'response': 'The Danish eurodance group that had a single called "Barbie Girl" is Aqua. The song was released in May 1997 and became a huge hit across the globe. In 2002, the song resulted in a lawsuit, which was notable in the group\'s history. Aqua is best known for this breakthrough single, along with other successful songs like "Doctor Jones" and "Lollipop (Candyman)".', 'query': 'What Danish eurodance group had a single called "Barbie Girl" which resulted in a lawsuit in 2002?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Aqua is a Danish eurodance group, best known for their 1997 breakthrough single "Barbie Girl". The group formed in 1989 and achieved huge success around the globe in the late 1990s and early 2000s. The group released three albums: "Aquarium" in 1997, "Aquarius" in 2000 and "Megalomania" in 2011. The group sold an estimated 33 million albums and singles, making them the most profitable Danish band ever.', 'node_id': '5c879097-80a6-4a18-9135-466aa0e7c93e', 'score': 13.493202209472656}, {'text': '"Lollipop (Candyman)" is a song recorded by Danish dance-pop group Aqua. It was released as the fourth overall single from their debut album "Aquarium" as the follow-up to their most successful song "Barbie Girl" in Australasia, North America and Mainland Europe (it was not released in the United Kingdom.) Although it said to be one of the group\'s favorite songs, "Lollipop (Candyman)" failed to replicate the success of "Barbie Girl", "Doctor Jones" and "My Oh My" where it was released.', 'node_id': 'a8c89e22-9424-4360-921c-082625195e5f', 'score': 10.568252563476562}, {'text': 'Aquarium is the debut studio album by Danish-Norwegian band Aqua. The album was released in Scandinavia on 26 March 1997 and in the United States on 9 September 1997. Although the group had been together for three years under their original name Joyspeed, their only release under that name was a single called "Itzy Bitsy Spider". The album is best known for including the successful singles "Barbie Girl", "Doctor Jones" and "Turn Back Time", the first of those being a huge hit across the globe.', 'node_id': '33a84f13-d114-4bc6-9f53-7c03b1b05333', 'score': 10.31700611114502}, {'text': '"Doctor Jones" is a song by Danish dance-pop group Aqua. Released as the band\'s fifth single overall, it was the follow-up to their most successful song "Barbie Girl" in many regions. "Doctor Jones" was a similarly pop-oriented hit which sold well across the globe and ended the assumptions that Aqua would be a one-hit wonder; although they would remain so in America as "Barbie Girl" was their only hit there until "Lollipop (Candyman)" was released and hit the top 40 on the Hot 100.', 'node_id': '5337af65-b60e-4f3b-9b17-32c76e08793c', 'score': 10.249855041503906}, {'text': '"Barbie Girl" is a song by the Danish-Norwegian dance-pop group Aqua. It was released in May 1997 as their third single overall, and the first United Kingdom release, it is included on the album "Aquarium". The song was written by Søren Rasted, Claus Norreen, René Dif, and Lene Nystrøm, and it was produced by Johnny Jam, Delgado, Rasted, and Norreen. It was written after Rasted saw an exhibit on kitsch culture in Denmark which featured Barbie dolls.', 'node_id': '3067d786-2aa5-436e-8bde-cc53e47d1015', 'score': 10.175699234008789}, {'text': 'René Dif (born 17 October 1967 in Copenhagen, Denmark) is a Danish musician, singer-songwriter, DJ and actor, best known as the male lead vocalist of the Danish eurodance group Aqua.', 'node_id': '35ccfe9a-b80c-4b7b-9d18-d59c5e1c5f31', 'score': 8.344147682189941}, {'text': 'Lene Nystrøm Rasted (born Lene Grawford Nystrøm on 2 October 1973), better known by her stage name Lene, is a Norwegian musician and singer-songwriter who is the lead vocalist of the Danish eurodance group Aqua.', 'node_id': '2038ff9c-bd44-4eee-b4dd-2af6ef12eac1', 'score': 7.20479154586792}, {'text': 'Søren Nystrøm Rasted (born Søren Rasted on 13 June 1969 in Blovstrød, Denmark) is a Danish musician, singer, songwriter and record producer. He plays keyboard, guitar and sings backing vocals. He is one of the four members of Danish eurodance group Aqua, and was married to the Aqua vocalist Lene Nystrøm.', 'node_id': 'ed696c08-2cea-4b10-8924-329621c10156', 'score': 7.1807050704956055}, {'text': '"Søndagsbarn" is a single by Danish hip hop group Suspekt featuring vocals from Danish band Lukas Graham. The song was released as a digital download in Denmark on 22 May 2015 through Tabu Records. The song peaked to number three on the Danish Singles Chart.', 'node_id': '1cd9ac53-b2d2-43ae-86ea-174de1bfcea5', 'score': 6.806960105895996}, {'text': 'Karl David Sebastian Dencik (born 31 October 1974) is a Swedish-Danish actor. He has acted in both Swedish and Danish films, and has also had major roles in English-language films including "Tinker, Tailor, Soldier, Spy" and " The Girl with the Dragon Tattoo".', 'node_id': 'ed4a910b-71f3-41f5-980e-e1ab417ed39c', 'score': 6.288843631744385}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 6.59844584017992, 'vram_usage': 0.0}
