, 'score': 0.8774008750915527}, {'text': 'Solidago rugosa, the wrinkleleaf goldenrod or rough-stemmed goldenrod, is a North American species of flowering plants in the sunflower family. It is widespread across eastern and central Canada (from Newfoundland to Ontario) and the eastern and central United States (Maine west as far as Wisconsin and Iowa, south to Florida and Texas).', 'node_id': '76024c7f-c2a6-419a-b442-b8dd3fa4c140', 'score': 0.9234358072280884}, {'text': 'Solidago rupestris , the rock goldenrod or riverbank goldenrod, is a North American species of flowering plants in the sunflower family. It is found in the eastern United States, found today in the States of Maryland, Virginia, Kentucky, and Tennessee. There are historical records of it formerly growing in Indiana and Pennsylvania as well, but these populations now appear to have been extirpated.', 'node_id': 'c3b93d02-4d13-47b1-bda9-83b063cccd70', 'score': 0.926397442817688}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 1.0450464431196451, 'vram_usage': 1.22412109375}
