ndar, who was the son of Khosrau I. His rule seems to coincide with other pretenders such as Hormizd VI so it is likely that he ruled a district or province rather than the Empire in its entirety. He was killed after a few days of reign.', 'node_id': 'b7309d35-8fd3-4062-aaff-a590c1700c08', 'score': 1.2835910320281982}], 'consistency_check': 'CONFLICT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'ENTAILMENT', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 0.6809486355632544, 'vram_usage': 1.21240234375}
