 71%|███████   | 356/500 [58:56<28:04, 11.70s/it] 71%|███████▏  | 357/500 [59:03<24:23, 10.24s/it] 72%|███████▏  | 358/500 [59:23<30:58, 13.09s/it]['modern-day New York City'] {'response': 'The characters from "Gargoyles the Movie: The Heroes Awaken," after being in an enchantedly petrified state for a thousand years, woke up in modern-day New York City. This setting serves as the backdrop for the series, where the gargoyles take on roles as the city\'s secret night-time protectors. The transition from their medieval Scottish origins to the bustling urban environment of New York City is a central theme of the story, highlighting their adaptation to a new world while maintaining their protective instincts.', 'query': 'What city did the characters from Gargoyles the Movie: The Heroes Awaken wake up in after being in an enchantedly petrified state for a thousand years?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Gargoyles the Movie: The Heroes Awaken is a direct-to-video animated film from The Walt Disney Company. The film is actually the five-episode pilot ("Awakening") of the animated television series "Gargoyles" edited into one long feature film, approximately 100 minutes in length. As a result, numerous scenes from the original broadcast episodes were cut due to time constraints. In addition, a number of scenes were also moved around and some dialogues were changed.', 'node_id': 'b5aa4614-f2f1-4edc-b4bf-1cd08f1c6422', 'score': 0.6784971356391907}, {'text': "Gargoyles is an American animated series produced by Walt Disney Television and Buena Vista Television, and originally aired from October 24, 1994 to February 15, 1997. The series features a species of nocturnal creatures known as gargoyles that turn to stone during the day. After spending a thousand years in an enchantedly petrified state, the gargoyles (who have been transported from medieval Scotland) are reawakened in modern-day New York City, and take on roles as the city's secret night-time protectors.", 'node_id': '37b208e2-309f-4af8-94eb-4c6f9494c7ce', 'score': 0.785069465637207}, {'text': 'The episodes were produced and aired in 1994, and the film was released to laserdisc and VHS in February 1995 and featured an interactive VHS/LD board game. As the pilot episodes have been released to DVD as part of "Gargoyles": Season 1, this feature is unlikely to be released independently again.', 'node_id': '4829ca58-512c-4ad1-a532-75556cb09c51', 'score': 1.159386396408081}, {'text': "Paris Awakens (French: Paris s'éveille ) is a 1991 French drama film directed by Olivier Assayas.This film has been music composed by John Cale.The film starring Judith Godrèche, Jean-Pierre Léaud, Thomas Langmann, Antoine Basler, Jacques Martin Lamotte and Ounie Lecomte in the lead roles.", 'node_id': 'e5b2ee5d-a499-4c82-9b42-3d2fc159490b', 'score': 1.1719632148742676}, {'text': 'Awake is a 2007 American conspiracy thriller film written and directed by Joby Harold. It stars Hayden Christensen, Jessica Alba, Terrence Howard and Lena Olin. The film was released in the United States and Canada on November 30, 2007.', 'node_id': 'ad4c5344-199d-4e35-ad9c-45da12377ed9', 'score': 1.2500017881393433}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'CONTRADICTION'}, 'latency': 1.638881953433156, 'vram_usage': 1.41162109375}
