 76%|███████▌  | 379/500 [1:03:04<22:34, 11.19s/it]['comparable to the seven Wonders of the World'] {'response': 'The provided context is insufficient regarding the specific criteria that subjectively qualifies the Houston Astrodome to be called the Eighth Wonder of the World.', 'query': 'What criteria subjectively qualifies the Houston Astrodome to be called the Eighth Wonder of the World?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'When opened, it was named the Harris County Domed Stadium and was nicknamed the "Eighth Wonder of the World".', 'node_id': 'd7f02b5e-2273-446a-8545-5eccc5f91232', 'score': 0.8682866096496582}, {'text': "The NRG Astrodome, also known as the Houston Astrodome or simply The Astrodome, is the world's first multi-purpose, domed sports stadium, located in Houston, Texas. Construction on the stadium began in 1962, and it officially opened in 1965.", 'node_id': '04f51db8-18bf-447b-8d71-9b89d3cf67cf', 'score': 0.9412285089492798}, {'text': 'It served as home to the Houston Astros of Major League Baseball (MLB) from its opening in 1965 until 1999, and the home to the Houston Oilers of the National Football League (NFL) from 1968 until 1996, and also the part-time home of the Houston Rockets of the National Basketball Association (NBA) from 1971 until 1975. Additionally, the Astrodome was the primary venue of the Houston Livestock Show and Rodeo from 1966 until 2002.', 'node_id': 'ebd5f43e-12a1-40e1-ae60-329c4e512b88', 'score': 1.2149090766906738}, {'text': 'By comparison, the Washington Monument is 554.612 ft tall, but remains the tallest stone monument in the world. The column is an octagonal shaft topped with a 34 ft Lone Star – the symbol of Texas. Visitors can take an elevator to the monument\'s observation deck for a view of Houston and the Battleship Texas (see USS\xa0"Texas" ).', 'node_id': '2e99a428-4fb9-4fff-a334-20f63b590e26', 'score': 1.2356622219085693}, {'text': "The 1968 Houston Oilers season was the team's ninth season. The club would play their home games in the Houston Astrodome. The Oilers would become the first team in professional football to play their games in a domed stadium.", 'node_id': '99c71acc-fc25-41d5-8233-74be56c604de', 'score': 1.2604706287384033}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'ENTAILMENT', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 0.7372957225888968, 'vram_usage': 1.27099609375}
