['comparable to the seven Wonders of the World'] {'response': 'The provided context is insufficient regarding the specific criteria that subjectively qualifies the Houston Astrodome to be called the Eighth Wonder of the World.', 'query': 'What criteria subjectively qualifies the Houston Astrodome to be called the Eighth Wonder of the World?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': "The NRG Astrodome, also known as the Houston Astrodome or simply The Astrodome, is the world's first multi-purpose, domed sports stadium, located in Houston, Texas. Construction on the stadium began in 1962, and it officially opened in 1965.", 'node_id': '04f51db8-18bf-447b-8d71-9b89d3cf67cf', 'score': 9.635995864868164}, {'text': 'When opened, it was named the Harris County Domed Stadium and was nicknamed the "Eighth Wonder of the World".', 'node_id': 'd7f02b5e-2273-446a-8545-5eccc5f91232', 'score': 8.043181419372559}, {'text': 'The film was shot on location in Houston, Texas. During the opening credits, shots of the downtown Houston skyline (with One Shell Plaza under construction) zoom toward the Houston Astrodome and Astrohall, with the emerging Texas Medical Center in the background. It was the first film shot inside the Astrodome.', 'node_id': '715ab0e2-9816-4b45-9c17-4b6337622c46', 'score': 7.873992919921875}, {'text': 'For the Last Time: Live From the Astrodome is the first live album released by George Strait in 2003. The title refers to the fact that this concert was the final event that took place at the Houston Astrodome.', 'node_id': 'ae654a52-d812-408c-8676-f645dd05f655', 'score': 7.130388259887695}, {'text': "The 1965 Houston Astros season was the franchise's first season in the Houston Astrodome, as well as its first season as the Astros after three seasons known as the Colt .45s. It involved the Houston Astros finishing in ninth place in the National League with a record of 65–97, 32 games behind the eventual World Series champion Los Angeles Dodgers. The Astros were managed by Lum Harris.", 'node_id': '38bbac33-0130-47e4-ba13-e0ffd713b678', 'score': 7.035522937774658}, {'text': 'The 1973 Astro-Bluebonnet Bowl, part of the 1973 bowl game season, took place on December 29, 1973, at the Houston Astrodome in Houston, Texas. The competing teams were the Tulane Green Wave and Houston Cougars, with each competing as a football independent. Houston won the game 47–7.', 'node_id': 'd36a4060-36c4-443b-886e-480462318e5f', 'score': 6.976309776306152}, {'text': "The 1968 Houston Oilers season was the team's ninth season. The club would play their home games in the Houston Astrodome. The Oilers would become the first team in professional football to play their games in a domed stadium.", 'node_id': '99c71acc-fc25-41d5-8233-74be56c604de', 'score': 6.755941390991211}, {'text': 'The Shreveport Steamer were a professional American football team in the World Football League. The franchise began the 1974 season in Houston, Texas, as the Houston Texans, who are in no way related to the current NFL team of the same name, playing their home games at the Houston Astrodome. Toward the end of the season the team relocated to Shreveport, Louisiana, and became the Shreveport Steamer. They played at the 30,000-seat State Fair Stadium, now named Independence Stadium.', 'node_id': '119247de-be96-4b03-894b-52e35e63c60d', 'score': 6.714130401611328}, {'text': 'It served as home to the Houston Astros of Major League Baseball (MLB) from its opening in 1965 until 1999, and the home to the Houston Oilers of the National Football League (NFL) from 1968 until 1996, and also the part-time home of the Houston Rockets of the National Basketball Association (NBA) from 1971 until 1975. Additionally, the Astrodome was the primary venue of the Houston Livestock Show and Rodeo from 1966 until 2002.', 'node_id': 'ebd5f43e-12a1-40e1-ae60-329c4e512b88', 'score': 6.178823947906494}, {'text': '"Fearless" peaked at #47 on the UK Albums Chart. Eighth Wonder split up in 1989, with lead singer Patsy Kensit going on to devote herself to her acting career.', 'node_id': '1a1c348a-5523-4c3a-8322-5f583d8bdb83', 'score': 5.599679946899414}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'ENTAILMENT', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 0.9732465334236622, 'vram_usage': 0.0}
