['Soha Ali Khan'] {'response': 'The lead actress in "War Chhod Na Yaar" who has also acted in Bengali and English-language films is Soha Ali Khan. She is primarily known for her work in the Hindi film industry but has also appeared in films in Bengali and English. This versatility in her acting career highlights her ability to perform across different languages and film industries.', 'query': 'Which lead actor/actress in War Chhod Na Yaar has also acted in Bengali and English-language films?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'War Chhod Na Yaar (English translation: "Quit the War, Dude") is a 2013 Hindi Indian war comedy film directed and written by Faraz Haider and dialogues are written by Deepak Kingrani. The film was announced on 30 March 2013 with a launch party at Novotel Hotel in the presence of the lead actors, Sharman Joshi, Soha Ali Khan, Javed Jaffery, Sanjai Mishra, Dalip Tahil and Mukul Dev who play important characters in the film.', 'node_id': '2884cbd2-6b7e-4c27-9254-e775dc6fa005', 'score': 15.23143196105957}, {'text': 'Soha Ali Khan Khemu (born Soha Ali Khan , 4 October 1978) is an Indian film actress, known primarily for her work in the Hindi film industry, although she has also acted in Bengali and English-language films.', 'node_id': '3a228dae-4359-46a7-a716-d1cc6635a990', 'score': 13.295315742492676}, {'text': 'Gita Dey (5 August 1931 – 17 January 2011) was a renowned actress in Bengali Tollywood films, theatre and Bengali folk theater. She became a stage artist at the age of 6 years. She came to the film industry in 1943. Her first film release was "Ahuti" (1941) as a child actress. She acted in over two hundred Bengali language films and over two thousand stage shows.', 'node_id': '57b6c8be-9150-469f-ad13-8236cea15983', 'score': 10.749436378479004}, {'text': 'Farida Jalal (born 1949) is an Indian actress, who has acted in over two hundred Bollywood films. Known primarily for her work in Hindi cinema, she has also worked in Telugu, Tamil and English-language films.', 'node_id': 'ae7db98f-2bfe-4eb8-b889-4bef8eba9262', 'score': 10.540949821472168}, {'text': 'Siddhartha Ramchandra Jadhav is an Indian actor and comedian. He is popular on television and has acted in Marathi and Hindi movies making him one of the most talented and successful actors in both Marathis films and television. He has acted in several Bollywood movies like "Golmaal" and "Golmaal Returns" but he asserts that his first love is Marathi film, TV and stage.Jadhav also acted in a bengali movie named Ami Subhah Bolchi having Mithun chakraborty as the lead.', 'node_id': '53c0aa7c-5e7a-450f-a009-6699cd919699', 'score': 10.150808334350586}, {'text': 'Debashree Roy is an Indian actress who has performed in over hundred films. She is a National Award winner actress and known for her work in Bengali cinema. She has been a highly successful leading actress in Bengali cinema throughout eighties and nineties as well as a critically acclaimed actress. She started her career as a child artist in a Bengali film named "Pagal Thakur" (1966) directed by Hiranmoy Sen. She was launched as an adult actress in Arabinda Mukhopadhyay\'s Bengali flick "Nadi Theke Sagare" (1978).', 'node_id': 'c1af06ef-09a9-42ab-b845-c2daf34844e6', 'score': 10.066861152648926}, {'text': 'Karl David Sebastian Dencik (born 31 October 1974) is a Swedish-Danish actor. He has acted in both Swedish and Danish films, and has also had major roles in English-language films including "Tinker, Tailor, Soldier, Spy" and " The Girl with the Dragon Tattoo".', 'node_id': 'ed4a910b-71f3-41f5-980e-e1ab417ed39c', 'score': 9.770820617675781}, {'text': 'Anil Chatterjee (Chattopadhyay) Bengali: অনিল চ্যাটার্জী (চট্টোপাধ্যায়) (25 October 1929 – 17 March 1996) was a Bengali actor in the Bengali cinema during the early fifties through the mid-nineties and is mostly remembered as a character actor. He acted or performed in about 150 movies, including a few in Hindi.', 'node_id': 'a97a1f9c-4fc0-4d4a-ac15-d2315874a821', 'score': 8.133073806762695}, {'text': 'Maharshi Raghava (born "Raghava Gogineni") is an Indian actor from Andhra Pradesh. He acted in more than 170 films in various roles. He shot into fame as a lead actor with his first film "Maharshi". The same film earned him the title "Maharshi". He also acted in TV serials.', 'node_id': '15b00005-8101-46ad-8d2c-5ffcb0465333', 'score': 7.8941144943237305}, {'text': "Nagesh Bhosle (also Nagesh Bhonsle or Nagesh Bhosale) is an award-winning Indian film, television and theatre actor. He has recently worked on a Hollywood film called 'Hotel Mumbai' alongside Jason Isaacs, Armie Hammer and Dev Patel. Nagesh has acted in more than a hundred Indian films and thousands of episodes in Television shows. After completing endless projects in the Hindi, Marathi and Telugu language fraternity as an actor, he ventured into Directing and Producing. He has successfully made 6 films so far, as a Director.", 'node_id': '445e3374-34f4-49f6-b51a-11593e1ebc88', 'score': 7.484627723693848}], 'consistency_check': 'CONSISTENT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 5.9643536396324635, 'vram_usage': 0.0}
