['51,271'] {'response': 'The provided context is insufficient regarding the 2010 population of the city 2.1 miles southwest of Marietta Air Force Station.', 'query': 'What is the 2010 population of the city 2.1 miles southwest of Marietta Air Force Station?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'RAF Warmwell is a former Royal Air Force station near Warmwell in Dorset, England from 1937 to 1946, located about 5 miles east-southeast of Dorchester; 100 miles southwest of London.', 'node_id': 'afc5412d-f826-4cd4-bddb-24aaccfe9f0d', 'score': 11.265546798706055}, {'text': 'Marietta Air Force Station (ADC ID: M-111, NORAD ID: Z-111) is a closed United States Air Force General Surveillance Radar station. It is located 2.1 mi northeast of Smyrna, Georgia. It was closed in 1968.', 'node_id': '4e9f9d8a-7b8a-4d4b-b858-37362fc488a2', 'score': 10.860251426696777}, {'text': 'Eldorado Air Force Station located 35 miles south of San Angelo, Texas was one of the four unique AN/FPS-115 PAVE PAWS, early-warning phased-array radar systems. The 8th Space Warning Squadron, 21st Space Wing, Air Force Space Command operated at Eldorado Air Force Station.', 'node_id': '963d8784-a697-400b-9e36-123b168aef68', 'score': 9.082971572875977}, {'text': 'The 302d Air Division is an inactive United States Air Force Division. Its last assignment was with Fourteenth Air Force at Marietta Air Force Base, Georgia, where it was inactivated on 27 June 1949.', 'node_id': '20abe86b-b9f3-44b5-aea1-461697899c66', 'score': 8.866578102111816}, {'text': "The Camp Pedricktown Air Defense Base was a Cold War Missile Master installation with an Army Air Defense Command Post, and associated search, height finder, and identification friend or foe radars. The station's radars were subsequently replaced with radars at Gibbsboro Air Force Station 15 miles away. The obsolete Martin AN/FSG-1 Antiaircraft Defense System,a 1957-vintage vacuum tube computer, was removed after command of the defense area was transferred to the command post at Highlands Air Force Station near New York City. The Highlands AFS command post controlled the combined New York-Philadelphia Defense Area.", 'node_id': '4558c43d-20a9-4ac5-a913-4de1e7d49f14', 'score': 8.374259948730469}, {'text': 'The 410th Bombardment Squadron is an inactive United States Air Force unit. It was last assigned to the 94th Bombardment Group. It was inactivated at Marietta Air Force Base, Georgia on 20 March 1951.', 'node_id': 'a9eed5de-f4e3-4941-be9d-757314daa07e', 'score': 8.28144359588623}, {'text': 'Topsham Air Force Station is a closed United States Air Force station. It is located 2.1 mi north of Brunswick, Maine. It was closed in 1969.', 'node_id': '502fed53-e74a-4c0d-aaae-bb099221e8b2', 'score': 8.00066089630127}, {'text': 'Royal Air Force Station Cottesmore or more simply RAF Cottesmore is a former Royal Air Force station in Rutland, England, situated between Cottesmore and Market Overton. The station housed all the operational Harrier GR9 squadrons in the Royal Air Force, and No. 122 Expeditionary Air Wing. On 15 December 2009 it was announced that the station would close in 2013 as part of defence spending cuts, along with the retirement of the Harrier GR9 and the disbandment of Joint Force Harrier.', 'node_id': '7eefde05-94ba-4212-b874-0ec311c47ddd', 'score': 7.74283504486084}, {'text': 'The 419th Flight Test Squadron is a United States Air Force squadron. It is assigned to the 412th Operations Group, Air Force Materiel Command, stationed at Edwards Air Force Base, California.', 'node_id': 'a91059f0-741e-4e42-8e76-894eb166af8b', 'score': 7.421558380126953}, {'text': 'The 514th Flight Test Squadron (514 FLTS) is a United States Air Force squadron. It is assigned to the Ogden Air Logistics Center (OO-ALC), Air Force Materiel Command, stationed at Hill Air Force Base, Utah.', 'node_id': 'a46ea0f8-2201-4cc5-bf39-f835ffa37b67', 'score': 7.291590690612793}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'ENTAILMENT', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 0.6505128275603056, 'vram_usage': 0.0}
