 85%|████████▌ | 426/500 [1:10:29<13:55, 11.29s/it] 85%|████████▌ | 427/500 [1:10:37<12:35, 10.36s/it]['Holston River'] {'response': 'The provided context is insufficient regarding the river system in Chilhowie, Virginia that was the starting place for most Longhunters.', 'query': 'Which river system in Chilhowie, Virginia was the starting place for most Longhunters?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'It is designated as a Florida State Canoe Trail, an Outstanding Florida Water, and an Aquatic Preserve by the Florida Department of Environmental Protection. The Wekiva River system is also one of the two rivers in Florida federally designated as a National Wild and Scenic River for its scenery, recreation, geology, and diverse habitats.', 'node_id': '3924fdb6-c635-406b-a172-3745b9fb0b5b', 'score': 1.2188419103622437}, {'text': 'During the steamboat era on the Missouri River, when low water prevented riverboats getting up to Fort Benton, the mouth of Cow Creek became a river landing and freighting depot, and it was the start of the Cow Island Trail by which freight was moved on to Fort Benton by going north up Cow Creek and then west. In 1877 the Nez Perce Indian Tribe, fleeing to Canada, had several skirmishes along Cow Creek including the "Battle of Cow Island", and several days later at a camp on Cow Creek the Nez Perce, thinking themselves now beyond the reach of the U.S.', 'node_id': 'b95a504b-1ed7-4664-999f-35e66fe7f2f6', 'score': 1.2253170013427734}, {'text': 'Sligo Creek is a free-flowing tributary of the Northwest Branch of the Anacostia River in Maryland. (The Anacostia, in turn, feeds into the Potomac River and eventually empties into the Atlantic Ocean via Chesapeake Bay.) The creek is approximately 9.1 mi long, with a drainage area of about 11.6 sqmi . It also inspired Katherine Paterson to write the Newbery Medal award-winning book Bridge to Terabithia.', 'node_id': '058d5b83-99b4-4441-809c-efd5b92b1493', 'score': 1.232424259185791}, {'text': 'The Northern Virginia Campaign, also known as the Second Bull Run Campaign or Second Manassas Campaign, was a series of battles fought in Virginia during August and September 1862 in the Eastern Theater of the American Civil War. Confederate General Robert E. Lee followed up his successes of the Seven Days Battles in the Peninsula Campaign by moving north toward Washington, D.C., and defeating Maj. Gen. John Pope and his Army of Virginia.', 'node_id': 'b354777b-6985-4866-9621-7f60bbcab659', 'score': 1.2397081851959229}, {'text': "The river flows west, turns north, and flows west again, through rugged terrain in the Coast Range of California. The East Branch is the South Fork Eel's largest tributary.", 'node_id': 'b7bd79ba-e0f0-4a0b-ad8a-892363f71d23', 'score': 1.2606916427612305}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 0.5903544817119837, 'vram_usage': 1.25927734375}
