1.1242666244506836}, {'text': 'Fought from 28 to 30 June 1651, the battle took place in the province of Volhynia, on the hilly plain south of the Styr River. The Polish camp was on the river opposite Berestechko and faced south, towards the Cossack army about two kilometers away, whose right flank was against the River Pliashivka (Pliashova) and the Tatar army on their left flank. It was probably the largest European land battle of the 17th century.', 'node_id': '3ae84d48-d481-4ee3-ad1e-686944be963c', 'score': 1.138116478919983}, {'text': 'Gen. George B. McClellan. It was the final battle of the Seven Days Battles during the American Civil War, taking place on a 130 ft elevation of land known as Malvern Hill, near the Confederate capital of Richmond, Virginia and just one mile (1.6\xa0km) from the James River. Including inactive reserves, more than fifty thousand soldiers from each side took part, using more than two hundred pieces of artillery and three warships.', 'node_id': '3c0ad3b0-3234-4a70-928c-b660d2598e5a', 'score': 1.1581395864486694}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'ENTAILMENT', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 0.6183643843978643, 'vram_usage': 1.32958984375}
