 93%|█████████▎| 467/500 [1:17:12<04:18,  7.84s/it]['Battle of Guam'] {'response': 'The provided context is insufficient regarding the Battle of Guam. However, it does mention that the Battle of Manila occurred on November 29, 1574, while there is no information provided about the Battle of Guam. Therefore, I cannot determine which battle occurred first based on the given context.', 'query': 'Which battle occurred first, the Battle of Manila or the Battle of Guam?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': "The Battle of Manilla (1574) was a battle in the Manila area mainly in the location of what is now Parañaque between Chinese pirates, led by Limahong and the Spanish colonial forces and their native allies. The battle occurred on November 29, 1574 when Limahong's fleet landed in the town of Parañaque and from there, began to assault the fortifications of Intramuros. Initially, the inhabitants where disorganized and Limahong's forces routed them. Furthermore, the Chinese killed the Master-of-Camp of the Spanish, Martin De Goiti.", 'node_id': '3a390bf3-fbf4-4b7b-87b5-5c3ba1beee5a', 'score': 0.7854228019714355}, {'text': 'The Battle of Yao (Japanese: 八尾の戦い , Hepburn: Yao no tatakai ) was a confrontation that took place in 1615 during the early Edo period in Japan. The battle occurred in 1615 during the Siege of Osaka, in which Tokugawa Ieyasu planned to destroy the Toyotomi clan. It was fought between the Tōdō clan and the Chosokabe clan.', 'node_id': '8fe1f745-0890-4ad3-9fbc-63f316253e6e', 'score': 1.0197035074234009}, {'text': "This caused them to delay their assault on Manila as Martin de Goiti's house was an obstacle in their march. However, upon the arrival of a certain Filipino hero called, Galo, resistance started to organize. Under Galo's command, they were able to resist China-born Limahong until Mexico-born Juan de Salcedo arrived from Ilocos with 300 Ilocano Warriors and Limahong was defeated and eventually forced to retreat. Thereafter Limahong abandoned his plans to invade Manila and instead, set up a temporary kingdom in Pangasinan.", 'node_id': '30b2115e-10dd-473b-8de3-477c84569c97', 'score': 1.060441493988037}, {'text': 'The Battle of Alhandic (Spanish: "Batalla de Alhandic" ), also known as Zamora\'s trench Battle ("Batalla del Foso de Zamora"), was a battle that occurred on August 5, 939 in the city of Zamora, Spain. The battle occurred when the troops of Abd-ar-Rahman III assaulted the walls of Zamora. The defending troops were those loyal to Ramiro II of León, King of the Kingdom of Leon.', 'node_id': '04ce2454-b4c3-4c8c-8089-07333d552427', 'score': 1.0900837182998657}, {'text': 'The battle resulted in Andalusian victory.', 'node_id': '6548475e-b67d-4f47-a3df-2a98d61b94ec', 'score': 1.1025655269622803}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 0.797080023214221, 'vram_usage': 1.20068359375}
