 '1a90e7b9-4680-42e7-9f2c-b4363ccf5c19', 'score': 1.1114158630371094}, {'text': 'Jean du Chatelet, also known as Baron de Beausoleil and Auffembach (1578, Brabant – c. 1645, The Bastille, Paris), was a mineralogist, mining engineer and dowser.', 'node_id': 'ab08801f-bec4-4ec0-b978-38523988b5b3', 'score': 1.1404750347137451}, {'text': 'Chiara R. Nappi is an Italian physicist. Her research areas have included mathematical physics, particle physics, and string theory.', 'node_id': '798ecaa2-6ac3-4eb0-9c35-e1bbf0cd5e0a', 'score': 1.2075557708740234}, {'text': 'The principal laws of association are contiguity, repetition, attention, pleasure-pain, and similarity. The basic laws were formulated by Aristotle in approximately 300 B.C. and by John Locke in the seventeenth century. Both philosophers taught that the mind at birth is a blank slate and that all knowledge has to be acquired by learning. The laws they taught still make up the backbone of modern learning theory.', 'node_id': '07b946e6-0922-4a9b-b689-cfeb3851cfd1', 'score': 1.2400579452514648}], 'consistency_check': 'CONSISTENT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 1.525386268272996, 'vram_usage': 1.29443359375}
